window.HANDBUCH_INDEX=[{"p":"index.html","a":"","t":"Willkommen","s":"Willkommen","x":"Eine eigene Mission auf yavin1 in BehavEd-Remake: rechts das Skript, in der Mitte die Karte, unten die Zeitleiste. Das Spiel steuert seine Szenen mit ICARUS-Skripten: Listen von Befehlen wie \"geh zu dieser Stelle\", \"spiel diesen Ton\", \"stell die Kamera dorthin\". Ravens Original-BehavEd baute diese Listen aus Knöpfen. BehavEd-Remake tut dasselbe, Datei für Datei verträglich, und bringt mit, was das Original nie hatte: die Karte in 3D, die Figuren auf ihren Wegen, die Kamera in ihren Einstellungen und eine Zeitleiste, die alles abspielt - bevor du das Spiel überhaupt startest."},{"p":"index.html","a":"wege","t":"Willkommen","s":"Wo anfangen","x":"Neu hier? Lies  und  - zehn Minuten, und jede weitere Seite ergibt Sinn. Gleich etwas bauen? Nimm eines der Tutorials unten. Du suchst etwas Bestimmtes? Tipp es oben links ins Suchfeld - es durchsucht alle Seiten und springt an die Stelle."},{"p":"index.html","a":"tutorials","t":"Willkommen","s":"Tutorials","x":"Besides the big mission there are 63 short tutorials - each shows one thing in three to six steps. All of them, with pictures: . Scripts                   Camera and timeline            Figures         Map and entities             Animation   Missions, models and settings            "},{"p":"index.html","a":"kann","t":"Willkommen","s":"Was das Programm kann","x":" Skripte aus der Befehlsliste bauen, jeden Wert in einem Dialog ändern, kopieren, verschieben, rückgängig - wie im Original-BehavEd.  Ein Skript als Baum sehen, als Graph, wer wen startet, oder als Spuren über die Zeit.  Die Karte in 3D mit Licht, Effekten und Modellen; hindurchfliegen, Entities wählen und verschieben.  Kameraeinstellungen als Schlüssel auf der Karte: mit dem Gizmo verschieben und drehen, selbst fliegen, in der Vorschau ansehen.  Die Szene abspielen, jeden Befehl in der Zeit sehen, Befehle ziehen, um ihren Zeitpunkt zu ändern.  Wege laufender Figuren und fliegender Schiffe: Griffe für Anfang und Ende, neue Punkte, gehen oder rennen, Blickrichtung.  Schiffe, Türen und Plattformen animieren - als move-Befehle oder als ROFF-Datei, hier gebaut und bearbeitet.  Eine ganze Mission mit allen Skripten öffnen, eine eigene bauen und sie in ein .pk3 packen, das das Spiel lädt. Nichts geht verloren. Jede Änderung lässt sich mit Strg+Z zurücknehmen, und Dateien werden erst beim Speichern geschrieben. Die Dateien des Spiels selbst werden nie verändert: Neues landet neben deinen Skripten oder in deinem eigenen .pk3."},{"p":"funktionen.html","a":"","t":"What BehavEd can do","s":"What BehavEd can do","x":"BehavEd-Remake writes ICARUS scripts - the scripts behind every cutscene and every scripted moment of Jedi Academy and its mods. It writes them exactly like Raven's original BehavEd, file for file, and then shows you what they do: on the map, in 3D, over time. Each section below links to the tutorials that practise it."},{"p":"funktionen.html","a":"skripte","t":"What BehavEd can do","s":"Write scripts like the original","x":"The command list, the script tree and the action column. Every command of the game in one list - double-click, drag or press Insert to add it.  Each value in its own field: lists of allowed values, names picked from the map, sounds you can play, expressions with get, tag and random.  Copy, move, comment out, undo every step - even one single step from the middle of the history. ,  Compile to the .ibi the game runs, with clear messages that jump to the wrong line.  Every command and every SET_ field explained: ."},{"p":"funktionen.html","a":"ansichten","t":"What BehavEd can do","s":"Three views of the same script","x":"Graph: what starts what. Tracks: the script over time. Classic is the tree of the original. Graph shows the mission as nodes - the player start, runners, characters, scripts - and lets you connect them by dragging. Spuren lays the script out over time, with the camera, every figure and the dialogue in rows. , "},{"p":"funktionen.html","a":"karte","t":"What BehavEd can do","s":"The map in 3D - as the game draws it","x":"The landing pad of taspir1 with the mission's entities. Maps load straight from the game's .pk3 files, with their shaders, lightmaps, fog, glow, effects, sky portals and mirrors. Fly through them, look from above, save views on number keys. Place entities with tiles, drag and turn them on the grid, edit every key in the inspector. , , , "},{"p":"funktionen.html","a":"kamera","t":"What BehavEd can do","s":"Cameras you can see and fly","x":"A camera path played through the camera. Each camera ( MOVE ) and PAN is a shot on the map with its path. Move and turn shots with the gizmo, put them where you are looking, or sit in a shot and fly it in pilot mode. Zoom, fade, shake and follow play in the view exactly as in the game. , , , "},{"p":"funktionen.html","a":"figuren","t":"What BehavEd can do","s":"Figures that walk their paths","x":"A figure in the middle of its walk, with its path. Characters spawn with their real models and animations and walk where the script sends them. Their paths have handles: drag a walk target, insert a point mid-walk, switch walk, run or walk backwards, set where a figure looks and which way it faces. , , , "},{"p":"funktionen.html","a":"zeit","t":"What BehavEd can do","s":"A timeline for the whole scene","x":"Dragging a block in the timeline: everything after it moves along. Play the scene with sound, at any speed. Every command is a block in time - drag it and everything after moves along, drag its edge to change a duration. , "},{"p":"funktionen.html","a":"animation","t":"What BehavEd can do","s":"Animation: move commands and ROFF files","x":"The Raven's Claw taking off on a ROFF path. Set keys over time for a door, a platform or a ship. behaved writes them as move commands or builds a ROFF file, and it turns the game's own ROFF files into keys you can change - as a copy, never touching the original. , , , "},{"p":"funktionen.html","a":"missionen","t":"What BehavEd can do","s":"Missions: from nothing to a .pk3","x":"Saving a mission: every file, every check. Start a mission on any map with one click, open the missions of the game or a mod, continue them from their folder. Mission speichern checks everything, compiles every script and packs one .pk3 with map, entities, scripts and ROFF files - ready for devmap. NPC waypoint networks are created and checked on the way. , , "},{"p":"funktionen.html","a":"modell","t":"What BehavEd can do","s":"Character models and their animations","x":"A character in the model view, with its animation list. Every character of the game with its skin, every animation with its frames - click to play, double-click to put it into the script. , , "},{"p":"funktionen.html","a":"werkzeuge","t":"What BehavEd can do","s":"The tools around it","x":"Find and replace in one script or in all open ones.  Tabs, bookmarks and a split view to compare scripts and copy across.  Backups on every save, a backup folder, revert any command to how it was.  Four languages, six themes, any interface size, every shortcut rebindable. ,  Checks for updates and installs them. "},{"p":"erste-schritte.html","a":"","t":"Erste Schritte","s":"Erste Schritte","x":""},{"p":"erste-schritte.html","a":"installieren","t":"Erste Schritte","s":"Installieren","x":"Lade die neueste BehavEd-Remake-….zip von der Release-Seite und pack sie in einen Ordner deiner Wahl aus - etwa neben dein Spiel. In Windows wird nichts installiert. Starte behaved.exe. Beim Start sieht das Programm auf GitHub nach einer neueren Fassung und bietet sie an; ohne Nachfrage wird nichts geladen (der Schalter steht unter Hilfe)."},{"p":"erste-schritte.html","a":"spielordner","t":"Erste Schritte","s":"Den Spielordner angeben","x":"Karten, Modelle, Klänge und die Skripte des Spiels liegen in seinen .pk3-Archiven. Öffne Bearbeiten → Spielordner und trage die Spielordner mit Spielordner hinzufügen ein: zuerst base, dann einen Mod wie Movie Duels (MD). Der unterste Ordner gewinnt, genau wie fs_game im Spiel base überschreibt. Die Spielordner: zuerst base, darunter der Mod - der unterste gewinnt."},{"p":"erste-schritte.html","a":"oeffnen","t":"Erste Schritte","s":"Etwas öffnen","x":"Es gibt mehrere Wege hinein. Die Startfläche im Tab Mission (solange keine Karte offen ist) bietet eine neue Mission, eine Mission aus einem .pk3, nur eine Karte und deine letzten Missionen an. Aus dem Menü: Eine Mission - Datei → Mission laden wählt ein .pk3 und öffnet eine Mission mit Karte, Entities und allen Skripten in Reitern. Siehe . Ein Skript - Datei → Öffnen öffnet eine .txt oder eine übersetzte .ibi von der Platte. Deine letzten Missionen - Datei → Zuletzt geöffnete Missionen öffnet eine ganze Mission mit einem Klick wieder. Die Startfläche erscheint im Mission-Tab, solange keine Karte offen ist."},{"p":"erste-schritte.html","a":"sprache","t":"Erste Schritte","s":"Sprache","x":"Das Programm spricht Englisch, Deutsch, Chinesisch und Japanisch. Es startet in der Sprache von Windows; umstellen lässt es sich unter Ansicht → Sprache. Befehlsnamen und Werte bleiben so, wie das Spiel sie schreibt (affect, SET_NAVGOAL), denn so stehen sie in der Datei. Dieses Handbuch öffnet sich mit F1, über Hilfe → Handbuch und Tutorials, über Erste Schritte und Tutorials auf der Startfläche und über den Knopf Handbuch in Ueber BehavEd. Es liegt im Ordner handbuch neben behaved.exe und braucht kein Internet."},{"p":"fenster.html","a":"","t":"Das Fenster","s":"Das Fenster","x":"Das Fenster im Mission-Tab mit einer offenen Mission."},{"p":"fenster.html","a":"bereiche","t":"Das Fenster","s":"Die Bereiche","x":"Menüleiste Datei, Bearbeiten, Debug, Ansicht, Hilfe - öffnen und speichern, Spielordner, Aussehen und Sprache, das Handbuch. Skript-Reiter Ein Reiter je offenem Skript. Ein * heißt: ungespeicherte Änderungen, + öffnet ein neues Skript, Reiter lassen sich umsortieren. Alle Reiter einer Mission teilen sich Karte und Kamera. Modusleiste Der Streifen ganz links: Ereignisse (Skripte bauen), Mission (die Mission: Karte in 3D, Entities, Kameras, Zeitleiste - bis rc599 hieß dieser Tab *Map*), Modell (ein Figurenmodell ansehen). Linke Spalte Hängt vom Modus ab: die Liste der Befehle, die Entities der Karte mit ihrem Inspektor oder die Animationen eines Modells. Skriptablauf Das Skript selbst - als Baum (Classic), als Graph (Graph) oder über die Zeit (Spuren). Siehe . Aktionen Die Knopfspalte rechts, wie im Original: bearbeiten, Datei, Baumoptionen, Übersetzen!. Im Tab Mission macht sie der Karte Platz. Zeitleiste Unter der Karte: spielt die Szene ab und zeigt jeden Befehl in der Zeit. Siehe . Statuszeile Meldungen, die Zähler für Fehler und Hinweise (anklicken zeigt die Liste), der Rückgängig-Verlauf und wann das Skript zuletzt übersetzt wurde."},{"p":"fenster.html","a":"teilen","t":"Das Fenster","s":"Zwei Skripte nebeneinander","x":"Datei → Geteilte Ansicht zeigt im Events-Modus bis zu vier Skripte nebeneinander - zum Vergleichen und zum Herüberkopieren von Befehlen. Einen Befehl von einem Feld ins andere ziehen kopiert ihn; in ein Feld klicken, um darin zu arbeiten."},{"p":"fenster.html","a":"groesse","t":"Das Fenster","s":"Größe, Aussehen und Aufteilung","x":"Strg + Mausrad skaliert die ganze Oberfläche (50 - 300 %); Ansicht → Bedienoberfläche skalieren tut dasselbe. Ansicht → Farbgebung: BehavEd klassisch, Windows, Dunkel, Mitternacht, Hell, Hoher Kontrast. Die Grenzen zwischen den Spalten ziehen ändert ihre Breite; jeder Modus merkt sich seine. Debug → Aufteilung zuruecksetzen stellt alles zurück. Eine Datei im Explorer öffnen, während BehavEd-Remake läuft, reicht sie an das offene Fenster weiter, statt ein zweites Programm zu starten."},{"p":"skripte.html","a":"","t":"Skripte schreiben","s":"Skripte schreiben","x":"Events-Modus: links die Befehle, in der Mitte der Skriptbaum, rechts die Aktionsknöpfe."},{"p":"skripte.html","a":"grundlagen","t":"Skripte schreiben","s":"Wie ein Skript aufgebaut ist","x":"Befehle laufen von oben nach unten. affect ( \"Name\", FLUSH ) { ... } schickt die Befehle darin an eine Figur oder Entity - so bewegt eine Zwischensequenz ihre Darsteller. task legt eine Gruppe von Befehlen an, do startet sie nebenher, dowait wartet auf sie, wait pausiert. if, else, loop wirken wie in anderen Sprachen. Nur affect, task, if, else und loop können Befehle enthalten."},{"p":"skripte.html","a":"einfuegen","t":"Skripte schreiben","s":"Befehle einfügen","x":"In der Liste Ereignisse links fügt ein Doppelklick einen Befehl hinter der gewählten Zeile ein (oder in den gewählten Block). Oder in den Baum ziehen: wo du loslässt, entscheidet, ob er vor, in oder hinter einer Zeile landet. Makros am Ende der Liste fügen mehrere Befehle auf einmal ein; Makros falten zeigt sie als eine Zeile. Ein Rechtsklick auf eine Zeile bietet dieselben Listen als Untermenüs, dazu bearbeiten, kopieren und Ähnliche suchen."},{"p":"skripte.html","a":"editor","t":"Skripte schreiben","s":"Der Event-Editor","x":"Ein Doppelklick auf eine Zeile (oder Enter) öffnet den Ereignis-Editor. Oben steht der Hilfetext des Befehls, darunter hat jeder Wert sein Feld: Listen für feste Auswahl, Zahlen- und Textfelder, Dateifelder mit  zum Suchen und Abspielen zum Abspielen eines Klangs oder Öffnen eines Skripts. Ist eine Karte geladen, wählt ein Pfeil neben Namensfeldern einen Namen aus der Karte. Der Event-Editor für einen Kamerabefehl. Ausdruck! macht ein Feld zum freien Ausdruck; Helfer baut get ( ... ), tag ( ... ) oder random ( ... ) mit Get, Tag und Rnd; Zurücknehmen geht zurück. Ein Wert, der nicht in seiner Liste steht, ist erlaubt - Mods bringen eigene mit - wird aber als unbekannt markiert, weil es viel öfter ein Tippfehler ist. Ok (Enter) schreibt die Werte, Abbrechen (Esc) verwirft sie, Neu auswerten setzt die Felder auf die Vorgaben zurück."},{"p":"skripte.html","a":"bearbeiten","t":"Skripte schreiben","s":"Wählen, verschieben, kopieren","x":"Klick wählt eine Zeile, Strg+Klick nimmt eine dazu, Umschalt+Klick wählt einen Bereich. Jede Aktion wirkt auf alles Gewählte. Zeilen ziehen verschiebt sie. Blöcke ziehen alles darin mit; ein Block kann nicht in sich selbst. Kopieren, Ausschneiden, Einfügen - Einfügen in einen Block setzt die Befehle genau einmal ein, auch wenn Block und Zeilen zusammen kopiert wurden. Klonen fügt direkt darunter eine Kopie ein, Auskommentieren macht Zeilen zu Kommentaren und zurück, Löschen entfernt sie. Rückgängig und Wiederholen merken sich jeden Schritt. Ein Rechtsklick auf einen der Knöpfe zeigt den ganzen Verlauf - dort lässt sich sogar ein einzelner Schritt zurücknehmen, während alles danach bleibt."},{"p":"skripte.html","a":"suchen","t":"Skripte schreiben","s":"Suchen, Ersetzen, Lesezeichen","x":"Suchen (Strg+F) öffnet ein Fenster, das offen bleibt: nach Befehlsnamen (Element mit Namen) oder nach einem Wert (Element enthält) suchen, mit F3 / Umschalt+F3 weiterspringen, in diesem oder allen offenen Skripten ersetzen. Lesezeichen wirken wie in Notepad++: Strg+F2 setzt eines, F2 springt zum nächsten. Sie bleiben je Datei erhalten."},{"p":"skripte.html","a":"rand","t":"Skripte schreiben","s":"Der Änderungsrand","x":"Mit Ansicht → Änderungsrand markiert ein farbiger Rand, was du geändert hast: orange = geändert, nicht gespeichert; grün = geändert und gespeichert; blau = wieder wie das Original. Darüberfahren zeigt die Originalzeile, Rechtsklick auf eine Zeile → Original wiederherstellen stellt nur diesen Befehl zurück."},{"p":"skriptfluss.html","a":"","t":"Script Flow: Classic, Graph, Spuren","s":"Script Flow: Classic, Graph, Spuren","x":"Die Knöpfe Classic / Graph / Spuren oben in der Spalte Skriptablauf schalten die Ansicht. In einer geteilten Ansicht hat jedes Feld seine eigene."},{"p":"skriptfluss.html","a":"classic","t":"Script Flow: Classic, Graph, Spuren","s":"Classic","x":"Der Baum des Original-BehavEd - jeder Befehl eine Zeile, Blöcke zum Aufklappen. Hier wird bearbeitet; siehe ."},{"p":"skriptfluss.html","a":"graph","t":"Script Flow: Classic, Graph, Spuren","s":"Graph: was startet was","x":"Der Graph einer Mission: Spielerstart, Auslöser, Skriptstarter, Figuren und Skripte mit ihren Verbindungen. Eine Mission wird von ihren Entities zusammengehalten: ein trigger zielt auf einen target_scriptrunner, der ein Skript startet, das Figuren steuert und andere Skripte startet. Genau das zeichnet der Graph. Doppelklick auf einen Knoten öffnet sein Skript oder zeigt die Entity in der Karte; vom Punkt rechts an einem Knoten zu einem anderen ziehen verbindet sie - bei einer Figur wählst du die Art des Skripts (spawnscript, deathscript, ...). Entities aus der Liste oder Befehle lassen sich in den Graphen ziehen; ein Befehl auf freier Fläche legt ein neues Skript an. Einpassen zeigt alles, Anordnen ordnet die Knoten, Rechtwinklig zieht die Leitungen rechtwinklig durch die Lücken. Doppelklick auf eine Leitung setzt einen Umlenkpunkt; Rechtsklick entfernt ihn."},{"p":"skriptfluss.html","a":"spuren","t":"Script Flow: Classic, Graph, Spuren","s":"Spuren: das Skript über die Zeit","x":"Spuren: Kameraeinstellungen, Figuren, Dialog und Skript als Blöcke in der Zeit. Eine kompakte Zeitleiste in der Skriptspalte: Zeilen für Kamera, jede Figur, Dialog (Sprachzeilen) und Skript. Klick auf einen Block wählt seine Zeile, seinen rechten Rand ziehen ändert die Dauer, im Lineal ziehen bewegt durch die Zeit. Die große  unter der Karte tut dasselbe genauer."},{"p":"speichern.html","a":"","t":"Speichern, Übersetzen, Prüfen","s":"Speichern, Übersetzen, Prüfen","x":""},{"p":"speichern.html","a":"speichern","t":"Speichern, Übersetzen, Prüfen","s":"Speichern","x":"Speichern (Strg+S) schreibt immer die .txt-Quelle - auch wenn du eine .ibi geöffnet hast (sie landet daneben). Alle sichern (Strg+Umschalt+S) speichert jeden geänderten Reiter; Reiter aus einem Archiv haben keine Datei zum Zurückschreiben und werden übersprungen. Jedes Speichern und Übersetzen behält eine Kopie - backup1.txt (neueste) bis backup10.txt - im Ordner backup neben behaved.exe, je Skript ein Unterordner; Datei → Sicherungsordner öffnen zeigt sie. Sicherung / Wiederherstellen halten von Hand eine zusätzliche Kopie fest (.bak neben dem Skript) und holen sie zurück. Eigene ROFF-Bahnen werden zusammen mit dem Skript als .rof-Dateien geschrieben - siehe ."},{"p":"speichern.html","a":"uebersetzen","t":"Speichern, Übersetzen, Prüfen","s":"Übersetzen","x":"Übersetzen! in der Aktionsspalte schreibt .ibi neben die .txt (und speichert die .txt). Der Knopf leuchtet grün mit Übersetzt oder rot mit Fehler - dann ist die erste fehlerhafte Zeile gewählt und die Statuszeile sagt, warum. Der Übersetzer ist eingebaut und wurde Byte für Byte an 1011 .ibi-Dateien aus Ravens IBIZE geprüft."},{"p":"speichern.html","a":"pruefen","t":"Speichern, Übersetzen, Prüfen","s":"Hinweise und Fehler","x":"Während du schreibst, prüft das Programm jede Zeile: unbekannte Befehle, Werte außerhalb ihrer Liste, ein Textfeld ohne Anführungszeichen, ein vertipptes Feld (\"meintest du ...?\"). Die Zähler in der Statuszeile zeigen, wie viele es sind - anklicken zeigt die Liste, ein Klick auf eine Meldung springt zu ihrer Zeile. Ansicht → Zielspiel ergänzt Hinweise, was auf einem Multiplayer-Server nicht geht."},{"p":"karte.html","a":"","t":"Die Karte","s":"Die Karte","x":"Die Kartenansicht mit ihrer Leiste oben und den Platzier-Kacheln links."},{"p":"karte.html","a":"laden","t":"Die Karte","s":"Eine Karte öffnen","x":"Schalte in der Modusleiste auf Mission. Eine Mission bringt ihre Karte mit (). Ohne Mission öffnet Karten  Dateien eine Karte von der Platte oder aus einem .pk3 oder lädt eine eigene .ent-Datei. Scripts (N) nennt die Skripte, auf die die Entities der Karte zeigen - eines wählen lädt seine Zwischensequenz."},{"p":"karte.html","a":"bewegen","t":"Die Karte","s":"Sich bewegen","x":"Fliegen; Q / E runter und hoch, Umschalt schneller W A S D (Maus über der Ansicht) Umsehen Rechte Maus ziehen Verschieben Mittlere Maus ziehen Umkreisen Alt + mittlere Maus Zoomen Mausrad Hinfliegen Doppelklick auf eine Entity in der Liste Ansicht merken; 1 ... 9 springt zurück (je Karte) Strg + 1 ... 9"},{"p":"karte.html","a":"anzeige","t":"Die Karte","s":"Was gezeigt wird","x":"Die Knöpfe rechts in der Leiste schalten Teile des Bildes an und aus: Entities, Namen, die Figuren des Skripts, Effekte, Glühen, dynamisches Licht, Nebel und Himmel. Draufsicht schaut wie eine Landkarte senkrecht hinunter und schneidet alles über der Schnitthöhe weg - die Höhe ziehen zeigt ein anderes Stockwerk. Ansicht einstellen (Zahnrad) enthält Helligkeit, Umgebungslicht, Detail, Figurenschatten und Entities dieses Skripts hervorheben, das alle Entities abblendet, die das aktive Skript nicht benutzt. Ansicht einstellen. Das Bild soll aussehen wie im Spiel: Shader, Lightmaps, Glühen (wie r_DynamicGlow), Nebel (r_drawfog), dynamische Lichter, Lens-Flares, Wetter und Klingenspuren. Statistik zeigt Bildrate, Texturen und Werte der Grafikkarte, wenn etwas falsch aussieht."},{"p":"entities.html","a":"","t":"Entities","s":"Entities","x":"Ein gewähltes Schiff: links die Liste, darunter der Inspektor, in der Ansicht das Gizmo."},{"p":"entities.html","a":"liste","t":"Entities","s":"Die Entity-Liste","x":"Die linke Spalte ordnet die Entities in Gruppen - Kameramarken, Laufziele, Blickziele, Figuren, Skriptstarter, Effekte, Klang, Bewegliches, Zerbrechliches, NPC-Wegpunkte. Das Auge blendet eine Gruppe in der Ansicht aus (Alt+Klick: nur diese zeigen), das Suchfeld filtert nach Name oder Klasse. Klick wählt, Doppelklick fliegt hin, Rechtsklick fügt einen Befehl für sie ein: Laufziel, Blickziel, affect-Block, Kamera zu dieser Marke."},{"p":"entities.html","a":"waehlen","t":"Entities","s":"In der Ansicht wählen","x":"Eine Marke, eine Figur oder ein Modell anklicken wählt es; Strg/Umschalt+Klick nimmt weitere dazu; ein über leere Fläche gezogener Rahmen wählt alles darin. Darüberfahren zeigt einen Kasten und den Namen. Die Leiste unter der Karte sagt, wie oft die gewählte Entity im Skript vorkommt, mit Knöpfen, die zu diesen Zeilen springen."},{"p":"entities.html","a":"gizmo","t":"Entities","s":"Verschieben und Drehen","x":"Eine kleine Leiste in der Ecke der Ansicht schaltet das Gizmo zwischen Verschieben und Drehen. Im Verschieben ziehst du die Entity über den Boden oder an einem der farbigen Pfeile; das in der Leiste eingestellte Raster rastet, Strg schaltet es beim Ziehen aus - ohne Raster rastet Strg einen Pfeilzug auf 8 Einheiten. Im Drehen gibt es Ringe (Strg: 15-Grad-Schritte): blau dreht links und rechts; Schiffe und Modelle haben dazu grün (nicken) und rot (rollen); Figuren nur den blauen, weil das Spiel für sie nur angle kennt. Alt+Ziehen kopiert zuerst. Mehrere gewählte Entities ziehen und drehen als Gruppe. Verschieben: nur Pfeile. Drehen: drei Ringe an einem Schiff. Steht die Zeitleiste mitten in einer Bewegung, ändert das Gizmo nicht den Anfang - es setzt an diesem Augenblick einen neuen Punkt. Siehe  und ."},{"p":"entities.html","a":"inspektor","t":"Entities","s":"Der Inspektor","x":"Unter der Liste zeigt der Inspektor die gewählte Entity: ihre Klasse mit einer Beschreibung aus dem Spielcode, Name, Position, Boden (wie hoch die Füße über dem Boden stehen - rot, wenn darin) und Blickrichtung (Grad), die Spawnflags als Kästchen und alle übrigen Keys als Felder. Skriptfelder haben Öffnen, NPC_type hat eine Suche über alle NPCs des Spiels. Die Symbolleiste fliegt hin, setzt sie Auf den Boden, dupliziert, löscht, animiert () und zeigt Alle Schlüssel (roh). Änderungen an Entities haben ihr eigenes Rückgängig, solange die Maus über der Karte oder der Liste ist."},{"p":"entities.html","a":"setzen","t":"Entities","s":"Neue Entities setzen","x":"Die Kacheln am linken Rand der Ansicht setzen die üblichen Arten: Figur, Laufziel, Kamera-/Blickmarke, Blickziel, Skriptstarter, Effekt, Klang, NPC-Wegpunkt, Spielerstart. Kachel anklicken, dann in die Ansicht klicken - oder die Kachel in die Ansicht ziehen; Umschalt setzt mehrere. + Entity über der Liste und ein Rechtsklick in der Ansicht (Neue Entity hier) bieten jede Klasse an. Der Knopf Raster rastet auf 8, 16, 32 oder 64 Einheiten."},{"p":"kamera.html","a":"","t":"Kamera","s":"Kamera","x":"Eine gewählte Kamera: ihre Bahn auf der Karte, das Gizmo, die Leiste oben und links die Liste der Einstellungen."},{"p":"kamera.html","a":"einstellungen","t":"Kamera","s":"Einstellungen","x":"In ICARUS ist eine Einstellung camera ( MOVE, ,  ) gefolgt von camera ( PAN, ,  ). BehavEd-Remake liest sie der Reihe nach und zeichnet jede als Kamerasymbol auf die Karte. Ein Klick auf das Symbol wählt die Kamera; die Liste Einstellungen links zeigt jede Einstellung mit ihrer Zeit und Fahrzeit (fährt 6,0 s). Ein Klick auf eine Zeile springt dorthin. Vorige Einstellung / Nächste Einstellung blättern durch die Einstellungen; Zur Einstellung fliegen stellt deine Ansicht genau dorthin, wo die gewählte Einstellung steht und hinschaut. Neue Kameraeinstellung hier fügt an deiner jetzigen Ansicht ein MOVE und ein PAN hinter der gewählten Einstellung ein. Auf Ansicht setzen setzt die gewählte Einstellung dorthin, wohin du gerade schaust. Einstellung löschen entfernt sie. Unter Gewählte Einstellung tippst du genaue Werte: Ort, Blickrichtung und Fahrzeit (0 = Schnitt)."},{"p":"kamera.html","a":"gizmo","t":"Kamera","s":"Eine Einstellung verschieben und drehen","x":"Die Leiste über der Ansicht schaltet das Gizmo um: Verschieben zeigt drei Pfeile und ein Kästchen in der Mitte - einen Pfeil ziehen verschiebt entlang einer Achse, das Kästchen in der Bildebene. Drehen zeigt drei Ringe für Nicken, Gieren und Rollen. Welt / Lokal entscheidet, ob die Pfeile der Karte oder der Kamera folgen. Beim Loslassen stehen die neuen Werte im Skript - ein Rückgängig-Schritt. Verschieben: Pfeile und das Kästchen in der Mitte. Drehen: drei Ringe. Steht die Zeitleiste beim Anfassen zwischen zwei Schlüsseln, entsteht an dieser Stelle ein neuer Schlüssel, statt den Anfang zu ändern - wie der Auto-Key in Animationsprogrammen. Beim Steuern setzt Enter ebenso einen Schlüssel ()."},{"p":"kamera.html","a":"bahnen","t":"Kamera","s":"Kamerabahnen","x":"Die gewählte Kamera zeichnet ihre Bahn: schon geflogene Stücke gelb, der Rest grau. Bei vielen Einstellungen wird das unübersichtlich - Aktive Bahn zeigt nur die Fahrt in die jetzige Einstellung und weiter zur nächsten, Alle Bahnen zeigt jede Fahrt. Beide Knöpfe stehen im Kamerafeld."},{"p":"kamera.html","a":"steuern","t":"Kamera","s":"Eine Einstellung selbst fliegen (Steuern)","x":"Steuern setzt dich in die Einstellung: rechte Maustaste halten zum Umsehen, W A S D zum Bewegen, Q E für runter und hoch. Übernehmen schreibt die Ansicht ins Skript, Esc bricht ab. Während du steuerst, die Zeitleiste weiterstellen und Enter drücken (Schlüssel setzen) setzt Schlüssel um Schlüssel entlang des Wegs."},{"p":"kamera.html","a":"vorschau","t":"Kamera","s":"Vorschau und Durchschauen","x":"Kameravorschau (in der Leiste der gewählten Kamera, oben links in der Ansicht) zeigt unten rechts ein kleines Bild aus Sicht der Kamera; es folgt dem Gizmo beim Ziehen. Ein Klick aufs Bild schaut groß durch die Kamera; dabei zeigt das Abspielen der Zeitleiste die Zwischensequenz so, wie das Spiel sie zeigen wird. Durch die Kamera in derselben Leiste tut das direkt. Durch die Kamera schauen, während die Zeitleiste läuft. Manche Einstellungen stehen auf einem ref_tag oder schauen auf einen. Dann sagt es das Feld, und das Verschieben der Einstellung verschiebt diesen ref_tag in der Karte - das Skript nennt ihn nur."},{"p":"zeitleiste.html","a":"","t":"Zeitleiste","s":"Zeitleiste","x":"Die Zeitleiste: oben die Kamerazeilen, je Figur eine Zeile, Unterzeilen nach Art, der Zeiger in Orange."},{"p":"zeitleiste.html","a":"abspielen","t":"Zeitleiste","s":"Abspielen","x":"Der Abspielknopf (▶) unter der Karte startet und hält an. Auf das Lineal klicken oder ziehen stellt die Zeit. Das Tempofeld verlangsamt die Szene (Ton nur bei 1x), Schleife wiederholt sie. Das Mausrad über dem Lineal zoomt, Strg+Rad über den Spuren ebenso; Alles zeigt alles, die mittlere Maustaste verschiebt. Bilder oder Sekunden - der Einheitenknopf schaltet um."},{"p":"zeitleiste.html","a":"zeilen","t":"Zeitleiste","s":"Zeilen und Arten","x":"Die Zeile Kamera enthält die Kamerabefehle (Fahrt, Schwenk, Zoom, Blende). Darunter hat jede Figur und jeder Mover, den das Skript anfasst, eine eigene Zeile. Ein Klick auf den Pfeil am Namen klappt sie auf: die Befehle sind sortiert nach Bewegung, Animation, Blick, Ton, Zustand und Ablauf (waits, Signale). Zeilen, in denen nach dem Start nichts geschieht, sind ausgeblendet; Ruhige Spuren zeigt sie. Die wait-Befehle sind zunächst ausgeblendet - sie setzen trotzdem alles in die Zeit, und das Verschieben eines Blocks passt sie an. waits zeigt sie als eigene Blöcke."},{"p":"zeitleiste.html","a":"ziehen","t":"Zeitleiste","s":"Zeit durch Ziehen ändern","x":"Einen Block nach links oder rechts ziehen ändert das wait davor - der Befehl kommt früher oder später, alles danach rückt mit. Einen Kamerablock an seinem Ende ziehen ändert seine Dauer. Laufen und Fliegen erscheinen als Bänder am unteren Rand der Zeile einer Figur; sie lassen sich genauso in der Zeit ziehen, ein Rechtsklick auf einen Lauf schaltet zwischen Gehen und Rennen. Ein Klick auf einen Block wählt seine Zeile im Skript, und die Karte springt zu diesem Augenblick - Zeitleiste, Skript und Karte zeigen immer dasselbe. Die Zeiten kommen aus einem Nachbau der ICARUS-Maschine des Spiels, samt ihrer Eigenheiten: ein wait endet ein Spielbild (50 ms) später als geschrieben, und ein dowait wartet auf die genannte Aufgabe. Lässt sich eine Zeit nicht wissen (ein waitsignal), sagt die Zeitleiste das, statt zu raten."},{"p":"figuren.html","a":"","t":"Figuren und Wege","s":"Figuren und Wege","x":"Eine laufende Figur: der Weg voraus in Grau, das schon gelaufene Stück in Gelb, die Griffe an Anfang und Ende."},{"p":"figuren.html","a":"folgen","t":"Figuren und Wege","s":"Figuren und Schiffe wählen","x":"Eine Figur oder ein Schiff in der Ansicht anklicken wählt ihre Entity - den Spawner der Figur, die Brush-Entity des Schiffs. Marke und Gizmo folgen dem Modell, während es sich bewegt, und ein Umriss zeigt, was gewählt ist. Der Pfeil an der Figur zeigt, wohin das Modell schaut."},{"p":"figuren.html","a":"griffe","t":"Figuren und Wege","s":"Anfang, Ende und neue Punkte","x":"Den Endgriff ziehen verschiebt das Laufziel (den waypoint_navgoal) oder das Ende eines Flugs. Den Startgriff ziehen verschiebt nur den Anfang, nicht die ganze Linie. Die Figur mitten im Lauf greifen (Zeitleiste zwischen Start und Ankunft) und ziehen: an diesem Augenblick entsteht ein neuer Punkt - ein neuer Navgoal bei Figuren, ein geteiltes move bei Schiffen. Drehen geht genauso: mitten in einem Flug legen die Ringe einen neuen Punkt mit den neuen Winkeln an; bei einer Figur schreiben sie set ( SET_ANGLES ) zu dieser Zeit - im Laufen gilt das beim Ankommen, weil das Spiel laufende Figuren in ihre Richtung dreht."},{"p":"figuren.html","a":"gangart","t":"Figuren und Wege","s":"Gehen oder rennen, geteilte Ziele","x":"Ein Rechtsklick auf den Endgriff eines Laufs (oder sein Band in der Zeitleiste) öffnet sein Menü: Gehen (ab diesem Lauf) / Rennen (ab diesem Lauf) - schreibt SET_WALKING bzw. SET_RUNNING vor den Navgoal. Dabei ansehen - die Figur dreht sich beim Laufen weiter zu einer anderen Figur (SET_WATCHTARGET). Rückwärts laufen (schaut zurück) - eine Blickmarke hinter dem Start lässt sie rückwärts laufen; In Laufrichtung schauen beendet das. Teilen sich mehrere Figuren einen Navgoal, würde das Verschieben alle verschieben. BehavEd-Remake merkt das und gibt diesem Lauf zuerst eine eigene Kopie des Ziels - die Statuszeile sagt, welche es angelegt hat. Rückwärtslaufen wird auch in vorhandenen Skripten erkannt: bewegt sich eine Figur entgegen ihrer Blickrichtung, spielt die Szene wie das Spiel BOTH_WALKBACK1 oder BOTH_RUNBACK1."},{"p":"animation.html","a":"","t":"Mover animieren und ROFF-Dateien","s":"Mover animieren und ROFF-Dateien","x":"Das Fenster Animation im ROFF-Modus und die Bahn des Schiffs auf der Karte."},{"p":"animation.html","a":"start","t":"Mover animieren und ROFF-Dateien","s":"Das Fenster öffnen","x":"Wähle eine bewegliche Entity - func_*-Brush-Entities wie func_static-Schiffe und func_door, misc_model_breakable, fx_runner - und drücke Animieren im Inspektor. Hat sie noch keinen script_targetname, bekommt sie einen, denn ein Skript kann nur bewegen, was einen Namen hat."},{"p":"animation.html","a":"schluessel","t":"Mover animieren und ROFF-Dateien","s":"Schlüssel","x":"Stell die Zeitleiste dorthin, wo die Bewegung beginnt, und drücke Schlüssel am Zeiger - der erste Schlüssel merkt sich, wo die Entity steht. Geh in der Zeit weiter und drück ihn noch einmal. Dann die neue Raute in der Ansicht ziehen (Umschalt: nur hoch und runter) oder Werte in die Tabelle tippen: Zeit, Ort, Richtung. Oder einfach das Gizmo: solange das Fenster diese Entity zeigt und die Zeitleiste am ersten Schlüssel oder danach steht, setzt Verschieben oder Drehen mit dem Gizmo einen Schlüssel am Zeiger (oder ändert den, der dort steht). Schlüssel löschen und Zum Schlüssel wirken auf die gewählte Zeile; Animation entfernen nimmt die ganze Animation aus dem Skript."},{"p":"animation.html","a":"arten","t":"Mover animieren und ROFF-Dateien","s":"Skript (move) oder ROFF-Datei","x":"Gespeichert als ein affect-Block mit move und wait am Anfang des Skripts scripts/.rof, abgespielt mit play ( \"PLAY_ROFF\", ... ) Zwischen den Schlüsseln jede Fahrt beginnt schnell und läuft langsam aus wie die Mover des Spiels (oder gleichmäßig mit Gleichmäßig) ein weicher Bogen durch alle Schlüssel (Weich) oder gerade Stücke Gut für Türen, Aufzüge, ein Schiff, das durchs Bild fliegt lange freie Flüge mit vielen Kurven, Effekte auf genaue Bilder Umschalten mit Skript (move) / ROFF-Datei oben im Fenster - die Schlüssel werden umgewandelt, nichts geht verloren. Im ROFF-Modus nennt das Feld Datei die Datei (zum Beispiel md_am/roffs/sta2); darunter steht, wie viele Bilder und Sekunden sie hat."},{"p":"animation.html","a":"roff","t":"Mover animieren und ROFF-Dateien","s":"Wie ROFF-Dateien funktionieren","x":"Eine ROFF-Datei (.rof, \"Rotation and Origin File Format\") speichert je Spielbild einen kleinen Schritt: wie weit sich die Entity in den nächsten 50 ms bewegt und dreht. Das Spiel addiert diese Schritte zu dem Ort, an dem die Entity steht, wenn PLAY_ROFF läuft - eine ROFF-Bahn ist also relativ: verschiebst du die Entity, wandert die ganze Bahn mit. Alle 108 Dateien des Spiels und von Movie Duels sind Fassung 2, alle bis auf eine mit 50 ms je Bild - und so schreibt BehavEd-Remake sie auch. Die Schlüssel, die du bearbeitest, stehen als Kommentarzeile im Skript direkt vor dem play; die .rof wird aus ihnen gebaut. Deshalb wirken Rückgängig, Kopieren und Einfügen auf ROFF-Bahnen wie auf jeden Befehl. Beim Speichern des Skripts wird die Datei als scripts/.rof in denselben scripts-Ordner geschrieben; Mission speichern packt sie ins .pk3 der Mission."},{"p":"animation.html","a":"bearbeiten","t":"Mover animieren und ROFF-Dateien","s":"Eine ROFF-Datei des Spiels bearbeiten","x":"Spielt ein Skript eine fertige ROFF auf der Entity ab, nennt das Fenster sie unter ROFF-Bahnen dieser Entity im Skript:. Bearbeiten zerlegt sie in Schlüssel - entweder gerade Stücke oder einen weichen Bogen, je nachdem, was mit weniger Schlüsseln auskommt -, bis auf eine halbe Einheit genau. Die Datei des Spiels wird nie überschrieben: du bearbeitest eine Kopie (…_2), und der play-Befehl zeigt auf sie. Ein Schiff fliegt seine ROFF-Bahn. In der Zeitleiste ist ein ROFF-Flug ein Band unter Bewegung; ziehen startet den Flug früher oder später."},{"p":"wegpunkte.html","a":"","t":"NPC-Wegpunkte","s":"NPC-Wegpunkte","x":"Das Fenster NPC-Wegpunkte und das Netz auf der Karte. Geöffnet wird es mit NPC-Wegpunkte in der Kartenleiste. Netz zeigen zeichnet die Wege: grün von Hand gesetzt (target), blau automatisch (Navgoals und Kampfpunkte), orange Sprünge (targetJump). Wegpunkte setzen: auf den Boden klicken - jeder neue Punkt wird mit dem vorigen verbunden. Umschalt+Klick beginnt einen neuen Weg, Esc beendet. Verbinden: zwei Punkte anklicken verbindet sie (Strg: ein Sprung); zwei verbundene anklicken trennt sie. Ein Punkt hat höchstens vier Verbindungen. Netz erzeugen verteilt Wegpunkte über den begehbaren Boden (Abstand: die Originalkarten nutzen etwa 230) und verbindet sie - ein Rückgängig-Schritt. Erzeugte entfernen entfernt nur diese, von Hand gesetzte bleiben. Netz prüfen findet, was das Spiel ablehnen würde oder NPCs nicht nutzen können; ein Klick auf ein Problem fliegt hin."},{"p":"missionen.html","a":"","t":"Missionen","s":"Missionen","x":""},{"p":"missionen.html","a":"laden","t":"Missionen","s":"Eine Mission öffnen","x":"Mission laden (Menü Datei oder die Kartenleiste) wählt ein .pk3 und nennt die Missionen darin - die Karten mit Skripten. Eine wählen, und alles ist eingerichtet: die Karte, ihre .ent mit den Figuren der Mission und jedes Skript der Mission in seinem eigenen Reiter; vorn steht das erste Skript, meist das Intro. Alle Reiter teilen sich Karte und Kamera. Die Missionen eines Archivs - Missionen auf derselben Karte stehen zusammen."},{"p":"missionen.html","a":"zuletzt","t":"Missionen","s":"Zuletzt geöffnete Missionen","x":"Datei → Zuletzt geöffnete Missionen und die Startfläche nennen die zuletzt geöffneten Missionen - aus einem Archiv oder aus einem Missionsordner. Ein Klick öffnet das ganze Projekt wieder: Karte, Entities und alle Skripte. Ein Eintrag, dessen Datei fehlt, fällt aus der Liste. Datei → Zuletzt geöffnete Missionen."},{"p":"missionen.html","a":"neu","t":"Missionen","s":"Eine neue Mission","x":"Neue Mission beginnt eine Mission auf einer beliebigen Karte. Wähle die Karte, gib der Mission einen Namen (Buchstaben, Ziffern und _; das Spiel lädt sie als maps/.bsp, also devmap ) und einen Skriptordner. BehavEd-Remake legt einen Spielerstart, einen Skriptstarter, das Intro-Skript und einen Missionsordner unter Dokumente\\behaved\\missions an. Das Intro läuft, wenn der Spieler erscheint. Der Dialog Neue Mission. Eine Mission, die nie gepackt wurde, lebt in ihrem Ordner; Missionsordner öffnen setzt sie nach einem Neustart fort."},{"p":"missionen.html","a":"speichern","t":"Missionen","s":"Eine Mission speichern","x":"Mission speichern zeigt, was ins Archiv kommt - jede Datei mit ihrer Größe - und prüft die Mission vorher: ein Skript, das eine Entity benutzt, das es aber nicht gibt, ein Skript, das sich nicht übersetzen lässt, kein Spielerstart, ein Ziel, das ins Leere zeigt, eine .str ohne ENDMARKER. Fehler (rot) müssen behoben werden, Warnungen (orange) dürfen bleiben. Speichern speichert alle Skripte, schreibt die .ent, übersetzt die Skripte, nimmt deine eigenen ROFF-Dateien mit und packt das .pk3 in den Spielordner. Der Dialog Mission speichern mit seinen Prüfungen. Das Archiv landet neben den anderen Mod-Archiven (zz_.pk3 im Movie-Duels-Ordner, damit es gegen ältere Dateien gewinnt). Starte das Spiel und tippe devmap  in die Konsole, um sie zu spielen."},{"p":"modell.html","a":"","t":"Modellansicht und Figuren","s":"Modellansicht und Figuren","x":"Modell-Modus: links die Animationsliste, in der Mitte das Modell, unten die Abspielleiste. Schalte in der Modusleiste auf Modell. NPCs nennt jede Figur des Spiels (aus den .npc-Dateien) - eine anklicken lädt ihr Modell und ihren Skin, wie das Spiel sie zeigt. .glm öffnen und Aus .pk3 öffnen ein beliebiges Modell. Linke Maus umkreist, mittlere verschiebt, das Rad zoomt; Drehteller, Knochen und Ansicht einpassen stehen in der Leiste. Die Liste Animationen links zeigt jede Animation des Skeletts mit ihrer Länge; filtern nach Name oder nach BOTH / TORSO / LEGS / FACE. Klick spielt sie; Doppelklick (oder Ins Skript) setzt set ( SET_ANIM_BOTH, \"…\" ) hinter die gewählte Zeile des offenen Skripts - SET_ANIM_UPPER bei TORSO- und SET_ANIM_LOWER bei LEGS-Animationen."},{"p":"tutorials.html","a":"","t":"Tutorials","s":"Tutorials","x":""},{"p":"tutorials.html","a":"projekt","t":"Tutorials","s":"The big one: your own mission","x":"All tutorials use the base game - the map taspir1 and its characters - so the pictures match what you see. Any other map, and any mod such as Movie Duels, works the same way. If the parts of the window are new to you, read  and  first."},{"p":"tutorials.html","a":"kurz","t":"Tutorials","s":"Short tutorials","x":"Each one shows one small thing in three to six steps - start with any of them. Scripts Camera and timeline Figures Map and entities Animation Missions and models"},{"p":"tut-projekt.html","a":"","t":"Your own mission: take-off on Taspir","s":"Your own mission: take-off on Taspir","x":"The finished cutscene, seen through its camera. This tutorial uses only the base game: the map taspir1 - the landing pad at the start of the Taspir III mission - with Kyle's ship, the Raven's Claw, and the characters Kyle and Rosh. You need nothing but Jedi Academy and BehavEd. Every picture on the following pages was taken while exactly this mission was built, step by step."},{"p":"tut-projekt.html","a":"teile","t":"Your own mission: take-off on Taspir","s":"The parts","x":""},{"p":"tut-projekt.html","a":"vorher","t":"Your own mission: take-off on Taspir","s":"Before you start","x":"Add the game folder once: Bearbeiten → Spielordner → Spielordner hinzufügen → the base folder of Jedi Academy (the one with assets0.pk3). See . If the window is new to you, read  first - five minutes. Everything can be undone with Ctrl+Z. The game files are never changed: your mission goes into its own folder and its own .pk3."},{"p":"tut-p1.html","a":"","t":"1 · Create the mission","s":"1 · Create the mission","x":""},{"p":"tut-p1.html","a":"schritte","t":"1 · Create the mission","s":"Schritte","x":"Open the start page. Switch the mode bar to Mission. Without a map, the tab shows the start page. New mission. Click Neue Mission erstellen. In the list type taspir1 and pick it. As Missionsname type taspir_tut - letters, digits and _. The Skriptordner is filled in by itself. Press Anlegen. Look at what you got. The map opens on the landing pad. behaved has added a target_scriptrunner next to the player start: when the player spawns, the script taspir_tut/intro runs. It is open in a tab - a short camera shot behind the player start. Switch off the original intro. taspir1 has its own start: its player start already triggers a runner with taspir1/preIntro, and the same trigger now starts yours too - both would play at once. Type t271 into the search box of the entity list - that is the runner of the original (its usescript is taspir1/preIntro) - select it and press Delete. The Graph view shows such connections at a glance (). Every map of the game works this way. Its own entities stay; remove what you do not want - it changes only your mission, never the game."},{"p":"tut-p2.html","a":"","t":"2 · Place the characters","s":"2 · Place the characters","x":""},{"p":"tut-p2.html","a":"schritte","t":"2 · Place the characters","s":"Schritte","x":"Look at the pad. Hold the right mouse button and fly with W A S D until you see the pad from the south, a little from above. Place Kyle. Click the tile Figur (NPC_spawner) on the left edge of the view, then click near the south edge of the pad. A character marker appears and is selected. Name him. In the inspector under the entity list set Name to kyle and NPC_type to Kyle (the ... button lists every character of the game). Auf den Boden puts him exactly on the ground. Place Rosh the same way beside him: Name rosh, NPC_type rosh_penin. Two walk targets. Click the tile Laufziel (waypoint_navgoal) and click in front of the ship - name it nav_kyle. A second one beside it: nav_rosh. Hold Shift while clicking to place several entities of one kind. More in ."},{"p":"tut-p3.html","a":"","t":"3 · Let them walk","s":"3 · Let them walk","x":""},{"p":"tut-p3.html","a":"schritte","t":"3 · Let them walk","s":"Schritte","x":"Write the walk for Kyle. In the intro script, after the camera lines, insert affect (double-click it in the Ereignisse list) and give it the name kyle. Inside it insert task named walk, and inside the task set ( SET_WALKING, true ) and set ( SET_NAVGOAL, nav_kyle ). After the task: dowait ( walk ) and set ( SET_LOOK_TARGET, rosh ). The same for Rosh - copy the block (Kopieren, Einfügen) and change the names: rosh, nav_rosh, look target kyle. Watch them walk. Drag the playhead in the timeline. Both walk at the same time - an affect block does not hold up the script. Click Kyle to see his path: grey ahead, yellow behind. Walk or run. Right-click the walk target at the end of his path: Gehen (ab diesem Lauf), Rennen (ab diesem Lauf), Rückwärts laufen (schaut zurück) or Dabei ansehen change how he gets there. A detour. Grab Kyle in the middle of his walk and drag him aside: behaved inserts a new walk target there, and his path bends around it. Why the task? SET_NAVGOAL only starts the walk. dowait waits until the task is done - until he has arrived - so he looks at Rosh only when he stands. More in ."},{"p":"tut-p4.html","a":"","t":"4 · The camera","s":"4 · The camera","x":""},{"p":"tut-p4.html","a":"schritte","t":"4 · The camera","s":"Schritte","x":"The first shot is already there - the template behind the player start. Select it in the Einstellungen list, fly out to a wide view of the pad from the south-east and press Auf Ansicht setzen: the shot is now where you are looking. A second shot. Fly down behind Kyle and Rosh, low, looking at the ship. Press Neue Kameraeinstellung hier and set its Fahrzeit to 4 seconds: the camera flies from the wide shot to this one while the two walk. Fine-tune in the view. The camera bar has Verschieben (arrows) and Drehen (rings). Releasing writes the change into the script. Or fly it. Steuern puts you into the shot: right mouse looks, W A S D move. Enter sets a key at the playhead, Übernehmen keeps it, Esc throws it away. Look through it. Kameravorschau shows a small picture of what the camera sees; click it to look through the camera."},{"p":"tut-p5.html","a":"","t":"5 · The ship takes off","s":"5 · The ship takes off","x":""},{"p":"tut-p5.html","a":"schritte","t":"5 · The ship takes off","s":"Schritte","x":"Select the ship. The Raven's Claw on the pad is a misc_model_breakable named ravensClaw. Click it on the map, then Animieren in the inspector. ROFF file. In the Animation window choose ROFF-Datei. The script gets a block that plays the file, and the first key is where the ship stands now. Set the keys. At 5 s press Schlüssel am Zeiger - the ship still stands. At 6.5 s drag it straight up a little: a key is set at the playhead. At 8.5 s drag it forward and higher, and tip the nose up with the ring. At 10.5 s it is far away and high. Watch. Play the timeline: the ship lifts off and flies away. Weich makes one curve through the keys. Saved with the script. Saving writes scripts/taspir_tut/roffs/ravensClaw.rof next to the script; Mission speichern packs it into the .pk3. Animating with move commands instead of a file: . Changing a ROFF of the game: ."},{"p":"tut-p6.html","a":"","t":"6 · Cut, shake, follow, fade","s":"6 · Cut, shake, follow, fade","x":""},{"p":"tut-p6.html","a":"schritte","t":"6 · Cut, shake, follow, fade","s":"Schritte","x":"Cut. After the second camera move insert a wait of 5 seconds, then a new shot from outside the pad, looking at the ship, with Fahrzeit 0 - a cut. Shake. Insert camera and choose SHAKE: strength 4, 2000 milliseconds - the engines start. Follow the ship. Two camera ( PAN ) commands with a duration turn the camera up after the ship while it climbs; a wait after each lets them finish. Fade out. camera with FADE: from 0 0 0 and 0 to 0 0 0 and 1 in 1500 ms - black. Then camera ( DISABLE ) gives control back to the player. Fix the timing. Play and watch. Drag blocks in the timeline: everything after moves along. Drag a right edge to change a duration. The whole scene. Turn on Durch die Kamera and play from the start."},{"p":"tut-p7.html","a":"","t":"7 · A second script","s":"7 · A second script","x":""},{"p":"tut-p7.html","a":"schritte","t":"7 · A second script","s":"Schritte","x":"A spawnscript key. Select Kyle, add the key spawnscript with the value taspir_tut/kyle_spawn (+ Schlüssel in the inspector). Open creates it. Press Öffnen next to the key: the script does not exist yet, so behaved creates it in the mission folder and opens it in a tab. A macro. Double-click standOnly at the end of the Ereignisse list: three set commands that make Kyle stand and ignore enemies. Add set ( SET_WEAPON, WP_SABER ). Side by side. Datei → Geteilte Ansicht → 2 shows the intro beside the spawn script. Drag lines from one to the other to copy them."},{"p":"tut-p8.html","a":"","t":"8 · Save and play","s":"8 · Save and play","x":""},{"p":"tut-p8.html","a":"schritte","t":"8 · Save and play","s":"Schritte","x":"Save mission. Press Mission speichern in the map toolbar. The window lists every file it will pack and checks the mission: errors in red must be fixed, warnings in orange may stay. Pack. Press Speichern: scripts are saved and compiled, the .ent with your entities and the ROFF are written, and zz_taspir_tut.pk3 goes into the game folder. Play. Start Jedi Academy, open the console (Shift+~) and type devmap taspir_tut. The cutscene runs as soon as you spawn. Next time. Datei → Zuletzt geöffnete Missionen opens the whole mission again - map, entities and both scripts. Share the .pk3 with others: it holds everything the mission needs. Players put it into their base folder."},{"p":"k-neues-skript.html","a":"","t":"Write a script from scratch","s":"Write a script from scratch","x":""},{"p":"k-neues-skript.html","a":"schritte","t":"Write a script from scratch","s":"Schritte","x":"Start an empty script. Click the + at the end of the tab bar (or Datei → Neu). A tab unnamed.txt opens; switch the mode bar to Ereignisse. Insert an affect block. In the Ereignisse list on the left, double-click affect. It appears in the tree, already open, because a block holds commands. Name the figure. Double-click the new line (or press Enter) to open the Ereignis-Editor. Type the name of the figure into the first field - with a map loaded, the arrow next to it lists every name of the map. Leave FLUSH and press Ok. Put a command inside. Click the affect line once, then double-click wait in the list: because the selected block is open, the command goes to the start of the block. Commands inserted after that follow it, in order. Save. Speichern (Ctrl+S) asks for a name the first time. Script names are lower case without spaces, for example my_first.txt."},{"p":"k-neues-skript.html","a":"tipps","t":"Write a script from scratch","s":"Gut zu wissen","x":"With a closed block selected, a new command goes after the block, not into it. Only affect, task, if, else and loop can hold commands."},{"p":"k-befehl-einfuegen.html","a":"","t":"Three ways to add a command","s":"Three ways to add a command","x":""},{"p":"k-befehl-einfuegen.html","a":"schritte","t":"Three ways to add a command","s":"Schritte","x":"Double-click. Select the line after which the command should come, then double-click the command in the Ereignisse list. That is how the original BehavEd worked. Insert key. Click a command in the list once (it stays highlighted), select a line in the tree and press Insert. Handy when you add the same command several times. Drag. Drag the command from the list into the tree. While you drag, a line shows where it lands: above a line, below it, or - on the middle of a block - inside the block. Right-click. Right-click a line: the submenus Ereignisse and Macros insert after that line - or into the block, if you right-clicked an open block."},{"p":"k-befehl-einfuegen.html","a":"tipps","t":"Three ways to add a command","s":"Gut zu wissen","x":"Hover over a command in the list to read what it does. Macros at the end of the list add several commands at once, for example walkOnly."},{"p":"k-werte-bearbeiten.html","a":"","t":"Change the values of a command","s":"Change the values of a command","x":""},{"p":"k-werte-bearbeiten.html","a":"schritte","t":"Change the values of a command","s":"Schritte","x":"Open the editor. Double-click a line or press Enter. The help text of the command is on top, each value has its own field. Pick from a list. Fields with fixed choices are lists you can also type into: start typing to filter. A value that is not in the list is allowed (mods bring their own), but it is marked unknown - check for a typo. Files and names. File fields have  to browse and Abspielen to play a sound or open a script. With a map loaded, an arrow next to name fields picks a name from the map. An expression instead of a value. Ausdruck! turns a field into free text. Helfer builds one for you: Get reads a variable (get), Tag the place or angles of a ref_tag (tag), Rnd a random number (random). Zurücknehmen goes back to a plain value. Done. Ok (Enter) writes the values, Abbrechen (Esc) leaves everything as it was. Under each field you see the value it had before (..... war)."},{"p":"k-zeilen-ordnen.html","a":"","t":"Move, copy and comment out lines","s":"Move, copy and comment out lines","x":""},{"p":"k-zeilen-ordnen.html","a":"schritte","t":"Move, copy and comment out lines","s":"Schritte","x":"Select. Click a line; Ctrl+click adds lines, Shift+click selects a range. Every action works on everything selected. Move. Drag the selection to a new place, or press Alt+Up / Alt+Down to move it one line - it stays inside its block. A block moves with everything inside it. Duplicate. Klonen (Space) inserts a copy right below - the quickest way to a second camera shot or a second walk. Copy between scripts. Kopieren (Ctrl+C), switch tabs, select a line, Einfügen (Ctrl+V). Pasting puts the commands below the selected line. Switch off without deleting. Auskommentieren (Backspace) turns the lines into comments; the game skips them. Press it again (or Ctrl+Backspace) to switch them back on."},{"p":"k-zeilen-ordnen.html","a":"tipps","t":"Move, copy and comment out lines","s":"Gut zu wissen","x":"Löschen (Delete) removes lines for good - but Ctrl+Z brings them back."},{"p":"k-rueckgaengig.html","a":"","t":"Undo anything - even one step from the middle","s":"Undo anything - even one step from the middle","x":""},{"p":"k-rueckgaengig.html","a":"schritte","t":"Undo anything - even one step from the middle","s":"Schritte","x":"Undo and redo. Ctrl+Z undoes the last change, Ctrl+Y redoes it. The Undo entry in the Bearbeiten menu names the step, for example *Undo: delete*. See the history. Right-click the Undo button in the action column (or Bearbeiten → Rückgängig-Liste). The list shows every step, newest at the top. Go back several steps. Click a step and press Bis hierher rückgängig: that step and all newer ones are undone. Undo one old step only. Click a step and press Nur diesen Schritt rückgängig: only that change is undone, everything you did after it stays."},{"p":"k-rueckgaengig.html","a":"tipps","t":"Undo anything - even one step from the middle","s":"Gut zu wissen","x":"Entities on the map have their own undo: Ctrl+Z acts on them while the mouse is over the map or the entity list. To take back a command to the state it had when the file was opened, right-click it → Auf Original zuruecksetzen."},{"p":"k-suchen-ersetzen.html","a":"","t":"Find and replace in all open scripts","s":"Find and replace in all open scripts","x":""},{"p":"k-suchen-ersetzen.html","a":"schritte","t":"Find and replace in all open scripts","s":"Schritte","x":"Open all scripts. For a mission, Mission laden opens every script in its own tab. Open Find. Suchen (Ctrl+F). The window stays open while you work. Search a value. Type the old name into Element enthält. Weiter (F3) and Zurück (Shift+F3) step through the hits. Tick Nur ganze Zeichenkette so that kyle does not also hit kyle2. Search a command. Element mit Namen finds commands by name, for example every camera. Both fields together find only commands that match both. Replace. Type the new name into Ersetzen durch and press Alle ersetzen in allen offenen Dokumenten. Each script gets one undo step."},{"p":"k-suchen-ersetzen.html","a":"tipps","t":"Find and replace in all open scripts","s":"Gut zu wissen","x":"Right-click a line → Ähnliche suchen fills the Find window for you: every command of this kind, or every command with one of its values."},{"p":"k-lesezeichen.html","a":"","t":"Bookmarks and the split view","s":"Bookmarks and the split view","x":""},{"p":"k-lesezeichen.html","a":"schritte","t":"Bookmarks and the split view","s":"Schritte","x":"Set a bookmark. Select a line and press Ctrl+F2 (Bearbeiten → Lesezeichen). A mark appears next to the line. Jump. F2 goes to the next bookmark, Shift+F2 to the previous one. Bookmarks are kept per file. Split the view. Open a second script, then Datei → Geteilte Ansicht → 2. The second script shows beside the first. Copy across. The right side is read-only, but you can drag lines from it into your script - they are copied. To edit the right one, click its tab."},{"p":"k-lesezeichen.html","a":"tipps","t":"Bookmarks and the split view","s":"Gut zu wissen","x":"The split view works in the Ereignisse mode; the map and model views need the room."},{"p":"k-uebersetzen.html","a":"","t":"Compile and fix errors","s":"Compile and fix errors","x":""},{"p":"k-uebersetzen.html","a":"schritte","t":"Compile and fix errors","s":"Schritte","x":"Compile. Press Übersetzen! at the bottom of the action column. It saves the .txt and writes the .ibi next to it. The button flashes green when it worked. When it fails. The button flashes red, the status line says *Compile failed*, and the first wrong line is selected in the tree. Read the messages. Click the red or yellow counter in the status line at the bottom: the Meldungen window lists every message. Each one names the line and what is wrong. Fix and compile again. Usually it is a value in the wrong form - text without quotes, a missing }, a comparison other than =  !. Fix it in the editor and press Übersetzen! again."},{"p":"k-uebersetzen.html","a":"tipps","t":"Compile and fix errors","s":"Gut zu wissen","x":"For a mission, Mission speichern compiles every script at once and refuses to pack while one does not compile. Every save and compile keeps a copy: Datei → Sicherungsordner öffnen shows the last ten."},{"p":"k-tasks.html","a":"","t":"Wait until a figure has arrived","s":"Wait until a figure has arrived","x":""},{"p":"k-tasks.html","a":"schritte","t":"Wait until a figure has arrived","s":"Schritte","x":"Why. An affect block runs beside the script - the script does not wait for it, so two figures in two blocks already walk at the same time. But inside a block, set ( SET_NAVGOAL ) only *starts* the walk: the next command follows at once, and the figure would turn or talk while still walking. Put the walk into a task. Inside the figure's affect block insert task and name it, for example walk. Move the SET_NAVGOAL (and SET_WALKING, if you use it) into the task block. dowait. After the task insert dowait ( \"walk\" ). It starts the task and waits until it is done - until the figure has arrived. Everything after it happens when the figure stands. Two things at once. do ( \"walk\" ) starts a task and goes on at once. Declare a second task - for example look with a SET_LOOK_TARGET - and start both with do. Later, wait ( \"walk\" ) waits for the first one. Check it in the timeline. Play the scene: what follows a dowait starts where the walk block ends. Drag the walk target, and the rest moves with it."},{"p":"k-tasks.html","a":"tipps","t":"Wait until a figure has arrived","s":"Gut zu wissen","x":"Commands marked with * in their help text (such as SET_NAVGOAL) finish their task only when the action is done - that is what makes dowait wait."},{"p":"k-signale.html","a":"","t":"Let two scripts wait for each other","s":"Let two scripts wait for each other","x":""},{"p":"k-signale.html","a":"schritte","t":"Let two scripts wait for each other","s":"Schritte","x":"Where to wait. In the script that should pause, insert waitsignal and type a name, for example door_open. Where to give the signal. In the other script, at the moment it should go on, insert signal ( \"door_open\" ). Check the names. Both must be spelled the same. Only one script can wait for a signal of a given name. See it in the timeline. Expand the figure's group in the timeline: the row Ablauf (waits, Signale) shows waits and signals as blocks."},{"p":"k-signale.html","a":"tipps","t":"Let two scripts wait for each other","s":"Gut zu wissen","x":"The timeline cannot know how long a waitsignal waits in the game - everything after it is placed as if the signal came at once."},{"p":"k-makros.html","a":"","t":"Use macros","s":"Use macros","x":""},{"p":"k-makros.html","a":"schritte","t":"Use macros","s":"Schritte","x":"Find them. The macros are at the end of the Ereignisse list, each with the number of commands it holds. Hover over one to read what it does. Insert. Double-click or drag a macro like a command. walkOnly, for example, makes a figure walk and ignore enemies and alerts - five set commands. Fold or unfold. Makros falten in the action column shows a macro as one line. Switch it off to see and change the single commands."},{"p":"k-pilot.html","a":"","t":"Fly a camera shot yourself","s":"Fly a camera shot yourself","x":""},{"p":"k-pilot.html","a":"schritte","t":"Fly a camera shot yourself","s":"Schritte","x":"Select a shot. Click the camera on the map or a shot in the Einstellungen list on the left. Start Pilot. Press Steuern on the camera bar. You now look through this shot. Fly. Hold the right mouse button to look around, W A S D move, Q / E go down and up, Shift is faster. Set keys along the way. Move the playhead in the timeline, fly to where the camera should be at that moment and press Enter (Schlüssel setzen). Repeat for more keys. Finish. Übernehmen writes the view into the script; Esc (Abbrechen) leaves it as it was."},{"p":"k-kamera-ansicht.html","a":"","t":"Put a shot where you are looking","s":"Put a shot where you are looking","x":""},{"p":"k-kamera-ansicht.html","a":"schritte","t":"Put a shot where you are looking","s":"Schritte","x":"Fly to the view you want. Right mouse button + W A S D. A new shot. Neue Kameraeinstellung hier adds camera ( MOVE ) and camera ( PAN ) at your view, after the selected shot. Or move an existing one. Select a shot and press Auf Ansicht setzen: position and direction are replaced, one undo step. Check. Durch die Kamera on the map toolbar shows what the selected shot sees, with its zoom and the black cinema bars."},{"p":"k-kamera-ansicht.html","a":"tipps","t":"Put a shot where you are looking","s":"Gut zu wissen","x":"Save views you come back to: Ctrl+1 … 9 stores the view, 1 … 9 jumps back. They are kept per map."},{"p":"k-kamera-marke.html","a":"","t":"Aim the camera at a mark on the map","s":"Aim the camera at a mark on the map","x":""},{"p":"k-kamera-marke.html","a":"schritte","t":"Aim the camera at a mark on the map","s":"Schritte","x":"Place a mark. Click the tile Kamera-/Blickmarke (ref_tag) on the left edge of the view, then click where the camera should stand. Give it a Name in the inspector, such as cam_door. Camera to the mark. Right-click the mark in the entity list → Kamera auf diese Marke (MOVE + PAN). Two camera commands are inserted that use the mark's place and angles. Move the mark. Drag the mark in the view or change its Position: the shot moves with it. Turn it. The mark's facing is the camera's direction. If the mark aims at a target, move the target to change the view."},{"p":"k-zoom-blende.html","a":"","t":"Zoom, fade to black and shake","s":"Zoom, fade to black and shake","x":""},{"p":"k-zoom-blende.html","a":"schritte","t":"Zoom, fade to black and shake","s":"Schritte","x":"Insert a camera command. Double-click camera in the Ereignisse list, then open it with Enter. The first field chooses what it does. Zoom. Choose ZOOM: the first number is the field of view (80 is normal, smaller is closer), the second the time in milliseconds to get there. Fade. Choose FADE: start colour and opacity, end colour and opacity (0 to 1), and the time. 0 0 0, 0 to 0 0 0, 1 fades to black. Shake. Choose SHAKE: strength 0 to 16 and the duration in milliseconds. The timeline shows zoom, fade and shake in their own rows under Kamera."},{"p":"k-neu-timen.html","a":"","t":"Retime a cutscene in the timeline","s":"Retime a cutscene in the timeline","x":""},{"p":"k-neu-timen.html","a":"schritte","t":"Retime a cutscene in the timeline","s":"Schritte","x":"Play it. Press ▶ under the map and watch. Switch Sound on to hear the dialogue you are matching the cuts against. Move a block. Drag a block left or right. Everything after it moves along, so the rest stays in sync. Hold Alt to move only this block. Change a duration. Drag the right edge of a block - a camera move, a wait - to make it shorter or longer. Step exactly. With the mouse over the timeline, Left / Right move the playhead by 50 ms, with Shift by one second. Check the script. Every drag changes a value in the script (a wait, a time). Click a block to see its line."},{"p":"k-neu-timen.html","a":"tipps","t":"Retime a cutscene in the timeline","s":"Gut zu wissen","x":"A warning sign on a camera block means it overlaps the next one - in the game the next move would start from where this one began, and the camera jumps."},{"p":"k-ansichten.html","a":"","t":"Look through the camera while you work","s":"Look through the camera while you work","x":""},{"p":"k-ansichten.html","a":"schritte","t":"Look through the camera while you work","s":"Schritte","x":"Through camera. Durch die Kamera on the map toolbar shows the picture of the selected shot, with zoom and cinema bars. The small preview. Kameravorschau on the camera bar puts a small picture of the camera's view in the bottom right corner - you keep flying freely. Click the picture to look through it. Follow. Mitfahren in the timeline moves your view along with the camera while it plays. Slow motion. The speed list next to the play button plays at 0.25x to 2x. Sound plays only at 1x."},{"p":"k-gangart.html","a":"","t":"Walk, run or walk backwards","s":"Walk, run or walk backwards","x":""},{"p":"k-gangart.html","a":"schritte","t":"Walk, run or walk backwards","s":"Schritte","x":"Show the path. Click the figure on the map or its name in the timeline. Its path appears: grey ahead of the playhead, yellow where it already walked. Right-click a walk target on the path. The menu offers Gehen (ab diesem Lauf), Rennen (ab diesem Lauf) and Rückwärts laufen (schaut zurück). Pick one. behaved writes SET_WALKING / SET_RUNNING before this walk. It counts from this walk on - later walks keep it unless you change them too. Watch. Play the timeline: the figure is faster, and the walk block in the timeline is shorter."},{"p":"k-ansehen.html","a":"","t":"Make a figure look at someone","s":"Make a figure look at someone","x":""},{"p":"k-ansehen.html","a":"schritte","t":"Make a figure look at someone","s":"Schritte","x":"While walking. Right-click a walk target on the path → Dabei ansehen → pick a figure. The figure walks and keeps its head on the other one. Standing. Right-click the target entity in the entity list → Dorthin drehen (SET_WATCHTARGET) (SET_WATCHTARGET) or Als Blickziel einfügen (SET_LOOK_TARGET) (SET_LOOK_TARGET). The command goes into the script after the selected line. Back to normal. Right-click the walk target → In Laufrichtung schauen. Check it. Play the timeline. The category Blick in the figure's group shows when it looks where."},{"p":"k-blickrichtung.html","a":"","t":"Turn a figure at a moment","s":"Turn a figure at a moment","x":""},{"p":"k-blickrichtung.html","a":"schritte","t":"Turn a figure at a moment","s":"Schritte","x":"Go to the moment. Move the playhead in the timeline to where the figure should face another way. Select the figure on the map and switch the gizmo bar to Drehen. Turn. Drag the ring. When you let go, behaved writes the facing at this time into the script (a SET_ANGLES), and the status line says *Facing … degrees at … s*. During a walk. Turning while the figure walks sets the facing for when it arrives."},{"p":"k-blickrichtung.html","a":"tipps","t":"Turn a figure at a moment","s":"Gut zu wissen","x":"If the time is not known - a waitsignal or dowait before - behaved says so instead of guessing."},{"p":"k-animation-abspielen.html","a":"","t":"Let a figure play an animation","s":"Let a figure play an animation","x":""},{"p":"k-animation-abspielen.html","a":"schritte","t":"Let a figure play an animation","s":"Schritte","x":"Load the figure's model. Switch to Modell and press NPCs: click a character - its model and skin load as in the game. Find an animation. Type into Animation suchen, for example TALK. BOTH, TORSO, LEGS filter by body part. Watch it. Click an animation: it plays. Wiederholen, the speed and the frame buttons help to look closely. Into the script. Select a line in your script first (inside the figure's affect block), then double-click the animation or press Ins Skript: set ( SET_ANIM_BOTH, \"…\" ) is inserted after that line. See it on the map. Switch back to Mission and play the timeline: the figure plays the animation at that point."},{"p":"k-dialog.html","a":"","t":"Add a line of dialogue","s":"Add a line of dialogue","x":""},{"p":"k-dialog.html","a":"schritte","t":"Add a line of dialogue","s":"Schritte","x":"Insert sound. Inside the figure's affect block, insert sound. In the editor choose the channel CHAN_VOICE and pick the file with ; Abspielen plays it. Hear it in the scene. Switch Klang on in the timeline and play: the line sounds at its moment. See it. The Spuren view (top of the script column) has a Dialog row - every voice line as a block, so you see where the cuts fall. Time it. A wait after the sound keeps the next command until the line is over. Drag the wait's edge in the timeline to fit."},{"p":"k-entity-setzen.html","a":"","t":"Place, move and turn entities","s":"Place, move and turn entities","x":""},{"p":"k-entity-setzen.html","a":"schritte","t":"Place, move and turn entities","s":"Schritte","x":"Place. Click a tile on the left edge of the view - for example Laufziel (waypoint_navgoal) - then click on the floor. Hold Shift to place several. Esc stops. Move. Drag the entity over the floor, or drag a coloured arrow to move it along one axis. Ctrl snaps to 8 units. Turn. Switch the gizmo bar to Drehen and drag the ring; Ctrl turns in 15 degree steps. Copy. Alt+drag makes a copy and moves it. Or press Duplizieren in the inspector. Onto the floor. Auf den Boden in the inspector puts it exactly on the floor below - the inspector shows how high the feet are."},{"p":"k-entity-setzen.html","a":"tipps","t":"Place, move and turn entities","s":"Gut zu wissen","x":"Raster on the map toolbar snaps everything to 8 to 64 units while dragging and placing."},{"p":"k-entity-finden.html","a":"","t":"Find an entity and fly to it","s":"Find an entity and fly to it","x":""},{"p":"k-entity-finden.html","a":"schritte","t":"Find an entity and fly to it","s":"Schritte","x":"Search. Type a name or class into the search box above the entity list, for example navgoal or kyle. Fly there. Double-click the row: the view flies to the entity and selects it. Hide groups. Click the eye in front of a group to hide it in the view; Alt+click shows only that group. Alle zeigen brings everything back. Names on the map. Namen on the map toolbar writes every name into the view."},{"p":"k-entity-felder.html","a":"","t":"Edit an entity's keys","s":"Edit an entity's keys","x":""},{"p":"k-entity-felder.html","a":"schritte","t":"Edit an entity's keys","s":"Schritte","x":"Select the entity. Click it in the view or in the list. The inspector under the list shows its class in colour; hover over it for a description from the game code. General. Name is how scripts address it, Position and Blickrichtung (Grad) where it stands and faces. Keys. Under Felder, change values or add one with + Schlüssel. For a character, the ... next to NPC_type searches every NPC of the game. Script keys have Öffnen to open the script. Everything as text. Alle Schlüssel (roh) shows all keys as plain text, like Hammer without SmartEdit."},{"p":"k-entity-felder.html","a":"tipps","t":"Edit an entity's keys","s":"Gut zu wissen","x":"Entity changes are kept with the mission: Mission speichern writes them into the .ent file."},{"p":"k-draufsicht.html","a":"","t":"Look at the map from above","s":"Look at the map from above","x":""},{"p":"k-draufsicht.html","a":"schritte","t":"Look at the map from above","s":"Schritte","x":"Switch on Draufsicht on the map toolbar. The view looks straight down; the wheel zooms, right or middle mouse and W A S D move. Cut away ceilings. Drag the cut height box at the top right: everything higher is not drawn. Lower it to look at a lower floor. Work as usual. Selecting, dragging and placing work in the top view too - handy for paths and waypoints."},{"p":"k-hell.html","a":"","t":"See better in dark maps","s":"See better in dark maps","x":""},{"p":"k-hell.html","a":"schritte","t":"See better in dark maps","s":"Schritte","x":"Open Ansicht einstellen (the gear on the map toolbar). Helligkeit lightens everything, Grundlicht lifts only the darkest areas - 0 is exactly like the game. Switch things off. Nebel, Effekte, Glühen and Himmel on the toolbar switch those parts off. Without the sky you can look into the map from outside. Only this script. Entities dieses Skripts hervorheben in the view settings dims every entity the active script does not use."},{"p":"k-tuer.html","a":"","t":"A door that opens","s":"A door that opens","x":""},{"p":"k-tuer.html","a":"schritte","t":"A door that opens","s":"Schritte","x":"Select the door. Click it in the view - doors and platforms are func_ entities. In the inspector press Animieren. Mode. In the Animation window keep Skript (move): the movement becomes move commands in the script. First key. Put the playhead where the door should start moving and press Schlüssel am Zeiger - this is the closed position. Second key. Move the playhead later (for example 2 seconds) and drag the door up or aside in the view: while the window is open, dragging sets a key at the playhead. Play. The door now opens in the timeline. Gleichmäßig makes it move at constant speed instead of easing out."},{"p":"k-tuer.html","a":"tipps","t":"A door that opens","s":"Gut zu wissen","x":"Animated entities need a name; behaved gives the door one if it has none."},{"p":"k-roff-bearbeiten.html","a":"","t":"Change a ROFF file of the game","s":"Change a ROFF file of the game","x":""},{"p":"k-roff-bearbeiten.html","a":"schritte","t":"Change a ROFF file of the game","s":"Schritte","x":"Select the entity that plays the ROFF (a ship, a boulder) and press Animieren. Edit. Under ROFF-Bahnen dieser Entity im Skript: press Bearbeiten next to the file. behaved turns the frames into a few keys - the game file stays untouched, you edit a copy with its own name. Change the keys. Drag the diamonds in the view, change times in the table, add keys with Schlüssel am Zeiger. Save. Saving the script writes scripts/.rof; Mission speichern puts it into the .pk3. Building a ROFF from scratch: . The details: ."},{"p":"k-graph.html","a":"","t":"Connect a character to a script","s":"Connect a character to a script","x":""},{"p":"k-graph.html","a":"schritte","t":"Connect a character to a script","s":"Schritte","x":"Open the Graph. Above the script column, switch from Classic to Graph. Every entity and script of the mission is a node. Drag a wire. Drag from the dot on the right of a character node to a script node. Choose when. A menu asks Verbinden als: spawnscript (when it appears), deathscript, usescript and more. behaved writes the key into the entity. New script. Drag a command from the Ereignisse list onto empty space in the graph: a new script with that command is made."},{"p":"k-mission-weiter.html","a":"","t":"Continue and pack a mission","s":"Continue and pack a mission","x":""},{"p":"k-mission-weiter.html","a":"schritte","t":"Continue and pack a mission","s":"Schritte","x":"Open it again. Datei → Zuletzt geöffnete Missionen, or the list on the start page of the Mission tab, opens map, entities and every script with one click. Missionsordner öffnen opens one from its folder. Work. Change scripts and entities. A dot next to the mission name means unsaved changes. Save mission. Mission speichern shows every file it will pack and checks the mission: errors in red (they must be fixed), warnings in orange. Pack. Press Speichern: scripts are saved and compiled, the .ent written and the .pk3 packed. Start the game with devmap ."},{"p":"k-wegpunkte.html","a":"","t":"Give NPCs paths to walk","s":"Give NPCs paths to walk","x":""},{"p":"k-wegpunkte.html","a":"schritte","t":"Give NPCs paths to walk","s":"Schritte","x":"Open the window. NPC-Wegpunkte on the map toolbar. Netz zeigen shows the network: green by hand, blue automatic, orange jumps. Create automatically. Press Netz erzeugen: waypoints are spread over the walkable floor and connected. The spacing slider sets how dense (the original levels use about 230). Check. Netz prüfen finds what the game would reject - click a problem to fly there. By hand. Wegpunkte setzen: click the floor to place a path; Verbinden connects two points (Ctrl: a jump). More in ."},{"p":"k-modell.html","a":"","t":"Look at a character model","s":"Look at a character model","x":""},{"p":"k-modell.html","a":"schritte","t":"Look at a character model","s":"Schritte","x":"Switch to Modell in the mode bar. Pick a character. NPCs lists every character of the game - type to search, click to load it with its skin. Look around. Left mouse turns, middle mouse moves, the wheel zooms. Drehteller turns it by itself, Ansicht einpassen brings it back to the front. Details. Haut switches skins, Knochen shows the skeleton, Texturen switches textures off."},{"p":"k-variablen.html","a":"","t":"Only the first time: variables and if","s":"Only the first time: variables and if","x":""},{"p":"k-variablen.html","a":"schritte","t":"Only the first time: variables and if","s":"Schritte","x":"Declare once. In a script that runs only once - the intro, a spawn script - insert declare, choose FLOAT and type a name, for example seen. A declared variable starts at 0; a map can hold 16 of them. Ask with if. In the script that may run more often (a trigger's script, see ) insert if. In the editor press Helfer on the first value and build get ( FLOAT, \"seen\" ) with Get; as comparison choose =, as the other value 0. Do it inside. Put the commands of the scene into the if block. An else right after it runs when the scene was already seen. Remember. At the end of the if block insert set with the variable name seen and the value 1 - next time the if is false. Free it with free ( \"seen\" ) when it is no longer needed, so the name is available again."},{"p":"k-variablen.html","a":"tipps","t":"Only the first time: variables and if","s":"Gut zu wissen","x":"Comparisons are =,  and ! (not equal) - behaved warns about anything else."},{"p":"k-patrouille.html","a":"","t":"A guard walks his round","s":"A guard walks his round","x":""},{"p":"k-patrouille.html","a":"schritte","t":"A guard walks his round","s":"Schritte","x":"Place the round. In the Mission tab place three or four walk targets with the tile Laufziel (waypoint_navgoal) (Shift places several) and name them round1, round2, round3. The guard. Place a character (Figur (NPC_spawner)), name it guard, and give it an affect ( \"guard\", FLUSH ) block in the script. Inside, insert the macro walkOnly first. The loop. Insert loop and keep -1 - forever. One leg per point. Inside the loop: a task with set ( SET_NAVGOAL, round1 ), then dowait for it, then wait ( 2000 ). Copy these three lines for each point and change the name. Play the timeline - the guard walks the round. Run instead. Replace walkOnly with runOnly - or right-click a walk target on the path and choose Rennen (ab diesem Lauf)."},{"p":"k-patrouille.html","a":"tipps","t":"A guard walks his round","s":"Gut zu wissen","x":"The macros patrolRun, patrolNoChase and patrolWalkNoChase set how a patrolling guard reacts to enemies."},{"p":"k-kamera-folgen.html","a":"","t":"Let the camera follow a figure","s":"Let the camera follow a figure","x":""},{"p":"k-kamera-folgen.html","a":"schritte","t":"Let the camera follow a figure","s":"Schritte","x":"Put the figure into a group. In the figure's affect block insert set ( SET_CAMERA_GROUP, \"hero\" ). Follow. After the camera shot insert camera and choose FOLLOW: the group hero, a turning speed (for example 100) and 1 to blend into it. The camera now keeps turning towards the figure. Keep a distance. camera ( DISTANCE, 200, 1 ) keeps the camera 200 units from the group, moving with it. Watch it. Play the timeline: the Follow row under Kamera shows how long it lasts, and the view turns with the figure."},{"p":"k-kamera-folgen.html","a":"tipps","t":"Let the camera follow a figure","s":"Gut zu wissen","x":"SET_CAMERA_GROUP_Z_OFS aims higher or lower on the followed figure."},{"p":"k-video-text.html","a":"","t":"Show a video or a line of text","s":"Show a video or a line of text","x":""},{"p":"k-video-text.html","a":"schritte","t":"Show a video or a line of text","s":"Schritte","x":"A video. Insert set and choose SET_VIDEO_PLAY; as the value type the name of a film in video/ without its ending - Jedi Academy plays .roq files this way, for example its intro jk0101_sw. Fade it. SET_VIDEO_FADE_IN and SET_VIDEO_FADE_OUT (true) set before the video let it fade. Text. print ( \"Three days later...\" ) shows a line in the middle of the screen."},{"p":"k-video-text.html","a":"tipps","t":"Show a video or a line of text","s":"Gut zu wissen","x":"behaved does not play videos in the timeline; it shows the command as a block so the timing stays visible."},{"p":"k-kampf.html","a":"","t":"Start a fight after the cutscene","s":"Start a fight after the cutscene","x":""},{"p":"k-kampf.html","a":"schritte","t":"Start a fight after the cutscene","s":"Schritte","x":"Calm at first. Give the enemy a spawn script (key spawnscript, Öffnen creates it) with the macro standOnly - he stands and ignores enemies. The scene. The cutscene runs as usual; the enemy can walk and talk like any figure. End the camera. At the end of the intro: camera ( DISABLE ) - the player plays again. Attack. Right after it, an affect ( \"enemy\", FLUSH ) block with set ( SET_IGNOREENEMIES, false ), set ( SET_LOOK_FOR_ENEMIES, true ) and set ( SET_ENEMY, \"player\" ). The macro default resets all behaviour in one line. More than one. Copy the block for each enemy, or put the lines into a script of their own and start it with run."},{"p":"k-kampf.html","a":"tipps","t":"Start a fight after the cutscene","s":"Gut zu wissen","x":"SET_BEHAVIOR_STATE with BS_DEFAULT gives the figure back to its normal AI after scripted walking."},{"p":"k-spieler-sperren.html","a":"","t":"Hold the player during a talk","s":"Hold the player during a talk","x":""},{"p":"k-spieler-sperren.html","a":"schritte","t":"Hold the player during a talk","s":"Schritte","x":"Lock. Insert affect ( \"player\", FLUSH ) and inside it set ( SET_PLAYER_LOCKED, true ). SET_LOCK_PLAYER_WEAPONS keeps the weapon as well. Talk. The other figures speak and move as usual; the player watches from his own view. Free. At the end the same block with false - otherwise the player stays frozen."},{"p":"k-spieler-sperren.html","a":"tipps","t":"Hold the player during a talk","s":"Gut zu wissen","x":"With camera ( ENABLE ) the game takes the controls away by itself; the lock is for moments without a cutscene camera."},{"p":"k-lichtschwert.html","a":"","t":"Ignite a lightsaber in a scene","s":"Ignite a lightsaber in a scene","x":""},{"p":"k-lichtschwert.html","a":"schritte","t":"Ignite a lightsaber in a scene","s":"Schritte","x":"The weapon. In the figure's affect block (or its spawn script): set ( SET_WEAPON, WP_SABER ). On. Where it should ignite: set ( SET_SABERACTIVE, true ). In the timeline the blade appears at that moment - with its sound when Klang is on. Off. set ( SET_SABERACTIVE, false )."},{"p":"k-lichtschwert.html","a":"tipps","t":"Ignite a lightsaber in a scene","s":"Gut zu wissen","x":"SET_SABER1 gives the figure another saber by its name from the game's saber files."},{"p":"k-trigger.html","a":"","t":"Start a scene when the player walks somewhere","s":"Start a scene when the player walks somewhere","x":""},{"p":"k-trigger.html","a":"schritte","t":"Start a scene when the player walks somewhere","s":"Schritte","x":"A runner. In the Mission tab click the tile Skriptstarter (target_scriptrunner) and click near the place. behaved names it and sets its usescript to a script in your mission folder. Its script. In the inspector press Öffnen next to usescript: the script is created and opened. Write the scene in it. Find a trigger. Triggers are brushes of the map: type trigger into the search box of the entity list and pick one where the player passes. Fly there with a double-click. Point it at the runner. In the trigger's inspector set its key target to the runner's name. The Graph view now shows the arrow from trigger to runner to script. Once or every time. A runner runs once; its key count set to -1 runs it every time. For only-the-first-time logic see ."},{"p":"k-trigger.html","a":"tipps","t":"Start a scene when the player walks somewhere","s":"Gut zu wissen","x":"New trigger areas need brushes, which are made in a map editor - behaved can change every trigger of a map, but not draw a new one. A script can also start a runner directly with use."},{"p":"k-tuer-use.html","a":"","t":"Open a door from the script","s":"Open a door from the script","x":""},{"p":"k-tuer-use.html","a":"schritte","t":"Open a door from the script","s":"Schritte","x":"Find the door. Doors are in the group Movable (func_*) of the entity list. Click one to see it in the inspector. Its name. The door needs a targetname. A door with a name waits to be used instead of opening when someone walks up - which is what a scripted door should do. Insert use. Select the line in the script after which the door should open, then right-click the door in the entity list → use einfügen: use ( \"door1\" ) is inserted. Hear it. The door plays its own sounds (its soundSet). Play the timeline to check the moment."},{"p":"k-tuer-use.html","a":"tipps","t":"Open a door from the script","s":"Gut zu wissen","x":"Moving the door yourself instead - other distance, other speed: ."},{"p":"k-levelwechsel.html","a":"","t":"Go to the next map at the end","s":"Go to the next map at the end","x":""},{"p":"k-levelwechsel.html","a":"schritte","t":"Go to the next map at the end","s":"Schritte","x":"Place it. + Entity → Kartenwechsel (target_level_change). In the inspector set mapname to the next map (for example taspir2) and give it a Name such as next_map. Use it. At the end of the script: use ( \"next_map\" ) (right-click the entity → use einfügen). Check it. Mission speichern warns when a target points to nothing; play the mission to see the loading screen."},{"p":"k-effekt-musik.html","a":"","t":"Add an effect and change the music","s":"Add an effect and change the music","x":""},{"p":"k-effekt-musik.html","a":"schritte","t":"Add an effect and change the music","s":"Schritte","x":"An effect. Click the tile Effekt (fx_runner) and click where it should appear. In the inspector set fxFile to an effect of the game (a path under effects/, for example env/fire), give it a name, and tick STARTOFF so it waits. Start it. In the script: use ( \"fire1\" ) at the right moment. Effekte on the toolbar shows effects in the view. Music. + Entity → Musik (target_play_music), set music to a music file and a name; use it from the script to switch the music. Dynamic music. set ( SET_MUSIC_STATE, ... ) switches the game's own music between its states, for example to action."},{"p":"k-szene-aendern.html","a":"","t":"Change a cutscene of the game","s":"Change a cutscene of the game","x":""},{"p":"k-szene-aendern.html","a":"schritte","t":"Change a cutscene of the game","s":"Schritte","x":"Open it. Datei → Mission laden, choose assets0.pk3 in the game's base folder and pick a map, for example taspir1. The map and all its scripts open in tabs. Find the scene. In the Mission tab, Scripts (N) lists the scripts the map uses - pick the intro. The timeline shows its camera. Change a shot. Select a shot in the Einstellungen list, fly to a better view and press Auf Ansicht setzen - or change a time in the timeline. Pack it. Mission speichern writes the changed scripts with the map into zz_.pk3. Archives load in alphabetical order, so zz_ wins over the game's own files. Undo it. Delete the zz_ file from the game folder and the game plays its original again - the game files are never touched."},{"p":"k-multiplayer.html","a":"","t":"Check a script for multiplayer","s":"Check a script for multiplayer","x":""},{"p":"k-multiplayer.html","a":"schritte","t":"Check a script for multiplayer","s":"Schritte","x":"Switch. Ansicht → Zielspiel → multiplayer. An MP badge appears in the status line. Read the notes. Click the notes counter in the status line: the Meldungen window lists every command that does nothing or works differently on a server - checked against the multiplayer game code. Switch back to single player when you are done; the script itself is not changed."},{"p":"k-oberflaeche.html","a":"","t":"Set up the program your way","s":"Set up the program your way","x":""},{"p":"k-oberflaeche.html","a":"schritte","t":"Set up the program your way","s":"Schritte","x":"Shortcuts. Bearbeiten → Tastenkürzel: click a shortcut, press the new key. Esc cancels, Backspace clears; a clash shows which action already has the key. Theme and language. Ansicht → Farbgebung (six themes, among them BehavEd Classic and High Contrast) and Sprache. Size. Ansicht → Bedienoberfläche skalieren, or Ctrl+mouse wheel anywhere outside the timeline. Columns. Drag the dividers between the columns; each mode keeps its own widths. Debug → Restore default layout brings them back. The guide. F1 opens this guide - also rebindable. All settings: . All keys: ."},{"p":"k-tod.html","a":"","t":"When the enemy dies, the door opens","s":"When the enemy dies, the door opens","x":""},{"p":"k-tod.html","a":"schritte","t":"When the enemy dies, the door opens","s":"Schritte","x":"Give the figure a deathscript. Select the enemy in the Mission tab. In the inspector add the key deathscript with a script name of your mission, for example taspir_tut/rosh_dies - or, in the Graph view, drag a wire from the figure to a script and choose deathscript under Verbinden als. Create the script. Press Öffnen next to the key: the script is created in the mission folder and opened. Open the door. In it, insert use with the door's name - right-click the door in the entity list → use einfügen does it for you. A wait before it lets the moment breathe. Other moments. The same works with painscript (hit), awakescript (notices the player), angerscript (starts fighting), fleescript and spawnscript."},{"p":"k-ansprechen.html","a":"","t":"The player talks to a figure","s":"The player talks to a figure","x":""},{"p":"k-ansprechen.html","a":"schritte","t":"The player talks to a figure","s":"Schritte","x":"Make it usable. In the figure's spawn script insert set ( SET_PLAYER_USABLE, true ) - otherwise the use key does nothing. The script for the talk. Add the key usescript to the figure (or connect it in the Graph view as usescript) and press Öffnen. Write the talk. Sounds on CHAN_VOICE, a SET_LOOK_TARGET at the player, perhaps a short camera. The figure says its lines every time the player presses use. Only once? Set SET_PLAYER_USABLE to false at the end of the usescript - or use a variable ()."},{"p":"k-zusammenspiel.html","a":"","t":"Let several scripts work together","s":"Let several scripts work together","x":""},{"p":"k-zusammenspiel.html","a":"schritte","t":"Let several scripts work together","s":"Schritte","x":"Split the work. Long scenes are easier in parts: the intro starts the next part with run ( \"taspir_tut/talk\" ) - the name as under scripts/, without ending. Hand over. Where the intro must wait for the other part, insert waitsignal ( \"talk_done\" ); at the end of the other script signal ( \"talk_done\" ). See both. Datei → Geteilte Ansicht → 2 shows the two scripts side by side; drag lines across to copy them. Keep the overview. The Graph view draws run connections between the scripts of the mission."},{"p":"k-pruefen.html","a":"","t":"Fix what Save mission reports","s":"Fix what Save mission reports","x":""},{"p":"k-pruefen.html","a":"schritte","t":"Fix what Save mission reports","s":"Schritte","x":"Open the check. Mission speichern lists every file it will pack and, below, what it found. Errors in red stop the packing until they are fixed; warnings in orange let you pack anyway - but read them. S001 (warning) - a script is missing. An entity names a script that does not exist yet; in the game nothing would happen. Select the entity and press Öffnen next to the key: the script is created. S002 (error) - a script does not compile. Open it and press Übersetzen!: the wrong line is selected (). S003 (warning) - no player start. The mission cannot start. Place one with the tile Spielerstart (info_player_start). S005 (warning) - a target points to nothing. A target names an entity that does not exist - often a leftover of the original map, like the one in the picture. S004 and S006. A missing ENDMARKER is added for you (warning); an invalid mission name is an error - letters, digits and _ only."},{"p":"k-ibi.html","a":"","t":"Open a compiled script of the game","s":"Open a compiled script of the game","x":""},{"p":"k-ibi.html","a":"schritte","t":"Open a compiled script of the game","s":"Schritte","x":"Find it. Datei → In .pk3 blättern, choose Skripte and type part of the name into Filter, for example taspir1/intro. Open it. Double-click the entry: the .ibi opens as a script in the current tab - commands, values and blocks, exactly as Raven wrote them. Open an empty tab first (+) if you want to keep the script you are working on; with unsaved changes behaved asks before. From disk. Datei → Öffnen opens .ibi files from a folder the same way. Change it. A script from an archive has no file yet - the first save asks where to put it. To ship a changed version of a game scene, see ."},{"p":"k-pk3.html","a":"","t":"Find files in the game archives","s":"Find files in the game archives","x":""},{"p":"k-pk3.html","a":"schritte","t":"Find files in the game archives","s":"Schritte","x":"Open the browser. Datei → In .pk3 blättern. It lists the files of every game folder you added. Choose the kind. Skripte, Karten or Modelle. The Archiv list narrows it to one .pk3. Search. Type into Filter - part of a name is enough. Open. Double-click: a script replaces the one in the current tab (behaved asks first if it has unsaved changes), a map loads, a model opens with its skin in the Modell tab."},{"p":"k-aenderungen.html","a":"","t":"See what you have changed","s":"See what you have changed","x":""},{"p":"k-aenderungen.html","a":"schritte","t":"See what you have changed","s":"Schritte","x":"The margin. Change a value: a coloured bar appears left of the line - orange for changed and not saved, green for changed and saved, blue for back to the original. Ansicht → Änderungsrand switches it on or off. What was it before? Hover over the bar: the original line is shown. Back to the original. Right-click the line → Auf Original zuruecksetzen: only this command goes back, everything else stays. Identical commands. Ansicht → Gleiche Befehle hervorheben marks every command that looks exactly like the selected one - handy for a camera that is used several times."},{"p":"k-backup.html","a":"","t":"Get an old version back","s":"Get an old version back","x":""},{"p":"k-backup.html","a":"schritte","t":"Get an old version back","s":"Schritte","x":"Automatic copies. Every save and every compile keeps a copy - the last ten, backup1.txt (newest) to backup10.txt. Datei → Sicherungsordner öffnen opens the folder. Your own backup. Sicherung (Alt+B) writes .bak next to the script - before a big change. Restore it. Wiederherstellen (Alt+R) goes back to the .bak, after a question. Smaller steps. For the last few changes the undo history is quicker: ."},{"p":"k-meldungen.html","a":"","t":"Understand the warnings","s":"Understand the warnings","x":""},{"p":"k-meldungen.html","a":"schritte","t":"Understand the warnings","s":"Schritte","x":"The counters. The status line counts errors and notes. Click a counter to open the Meldungen window. Read them. Each message names its code and the command. A misspelt value such as SET_WALKNG is reported as *not in SET_TYPES (kept unchanged)* - behaved keeps it, because mods bring their own values, but it is far more often a typo. Fix and check. Correct the value in the editor - the message disappears. Messages never change the script by themselves."},{"p":"k-gruppe.html","a":"","t":"Move many entities at once","s":"Move many entities at once","x":""},{"p":"k-gruppe.html","a":"schritte","t":"Move many entities at once","s":"Schritte","x":"Draw a frame. In the Mission tab drag over empty space in the view: every entity inside is selected. Ctrl or Shift adds to it. Move the group. Drag one of them, or use the arrows: all move together. Turn the group. Switch the gizmo bar to Drehen and drag the ring. Copy it. Alt+drag copies the whole group - Duplizieren in the inspector does the same."},{"p":"k-blickpunkte.html","a":"","t":"Remember viewpoints and camera paths","s":"Remember viewpoints and camera paths","x":""},{"p":"k-blickpunkte.html","a":"schritte","t":"Remember viewpoints and camera paths","s":"Schritte","x":"Store a view. With the mouse over the map press Ctrl+1 … 9; the status line confirms it. 1 … 9 jumps back. The views are kept per map. All paths or one. In the camera panel, Alle Bahnen draws every camera move of the script, Aktive Bahn only the one around the playhead - clearer in long scenes. Fly to a shot. Zur Einstellung fliegen puts your view next to the selected shot."},{"p":"k-spawnflags.html","a":"","t":"A figure that appears on cue","s":"A figure that appears on cue","x":""},{"p":"k-spawnflags.html","a":"schritte","t":"A figure that appears on cue","s":"Schritte","x":"Two names. A character spawner has NPC_targetname - the name of the figure, used by affect - and may have targetname - the name of the spawner itself. Wait for the cue. Give the spawner a targetname, for example rosh_spawner. In the game it then spawns its figure only when it is used. Call it. In the script: use ( \"rosh_spawner\" ) - from then on the figure exists and affect ( \"rosh\" ) reaches it. (The preview shows the figure from the start.) Spawnflags. The checkboxes under Spawnflags set the class's options; hover over one for what it does."},{"p":"k-ent.html","a":"","t":"Load a separate .ent file","s":"Load a separate .ent file","x":""},{"p":"k-ent.html","a":"schritte","t":"Load a separate .ent file","s":"Schritte","x":"Open it. Karten  Dateien → .ent öffnen loads an .ent file: its entities replace the ones of the map. Work as usual. The entities appear in the list and the view; change them like any other. Saved with the mission. Mission speichern writes the entities into maps/.ent in the .pk3 - the game loads it instead of the map's own."},{"p":"k-spuren.html","a":"","t":"Time a scene in the Tracks view","s":"Time a scene in the Tracks view","x":""},{"p":"k-spuren.html","a":"schritte","t":"Time a scene in the Tracks view","s":"Schritte","x":"Switch to Tracks. Above the script column choose Spuren: rows for Kamera, each figure, Dialog and Skript. Jump to a line. Click a block: its line is selected. Change a duration. Drag the right edge of a block. Move through time. Drag in the ruler; Abspielen plays."},{"p":"k-zeitleiste-plus.html","a":"","t":"The timeline in detail","s":"The timeline in detail","x":""},{"p":"k-zeitleiste-plus.html","a":"schritte","t":"The timeline in detail","s":"Schritte","x":"Waits as blocks. waits shows every wait as its own block - drag it to change it directly. Quiet rows. Ruhige Spuren also shows the rows where nothing happens after the start. Frames. Click the time display to switch between seconds and frames. Speed. The list next to the play button plays at 0.25x to 2x; sound only at 1x. Overlap warning. A warning sign on a camera block: it overlaps the next move. In the game the next one starts from where this one began, and the camera jumps - shorten one of them."},{"p":"k-skins.html","a":"","t":"Skins and skeletons of a model","s":"Skins and skeletons of a model","x":""},{"p":"k-skins.html","a":"schritte","t":"Skins and skeletons of a model","s":"Schritte","x":"Switch skins. In the Modell tab the Haut list shows the skins that come with the model; .skin öffnen loads another one. Surfaces. The counter of surfaces shows how many the skin draws; click it to list them all in the detail log. Caps. Kappen zeigen shows the _off surfaces that close the holes where limbs attach. Another skeleton. .gla laden loads a different .gla with its animations."},{"p":"einstellungen.html","a":"","t":"Einstellungen und Updates","s":"Einstellungen und Updates","x":""},{"p":"einstellungen.html","a":"spielordner","t":"Einstellungen und Updates","s":"Spielordner","x":"Bearbeiten → Spielordner nennt die Ordner, deren .pk3-Archive das Programm liest, je mit Hoch, Runter, Entfernen und Öffnen. Der unterste gewinnt gegen alles darüber, wie fs_game in der Engine base überschreibt. Ein Ordner ohne Archive sagt das - dann stimmt der Pfad nicht. Die Spielordner."},{"p":"einstellungen.html","a":"prefs","t":"Einstellungen und Updates","s":"Einstellungen","x":"Bearbeiten → Einstellungen (oder Einstellungen in der Aktionsspalte, Alt+P) enthält die Optionen des Original-BehavEd: Verzeichnisse: Skriptpfad, Befehlsbeschreibung (die .bhc, die jeden Befehl festlegt - Befehlsmodell neu laden liest sie neu), Quelldateien. Letzte Datei beim Start öffnen, Klapplisten alphabetisch, Zweiter Farbsatz für Symbole, Nachfragen bei Öffnen/Neu/Beenden, Dateidialog beim zuletzt benutzten Ordner öffnen. Sprache, Farbgebung und Oberflächengröße stehen im Menü Ansicht."},{"p":"einstellungen.html","a":"tasten","t":"Einstellungen und Updates","s":"Tasten ändern","x":"Bearbeiten → Tastenkürzel nennt jede Aktion mit Taste. Ein Kürzel anklicken und die neue Taste drücken; Esc bricht ab, Rücktaste löscht. Eine schon belegte Taste wird genannt. Die Vorgaben stehen in ."},{"p":"einstellungen.html","a":"updates","t":"Einstellungen und Updates","s":"Updates und Änderungsliste","x":"Hilfe → Nach Updates suchen fragt GitHub nach einer neueren Fassung und zeigt, was neu ist; Herunterladen und installieren ersetzt die Programmdateien und bietet einen Neustart an. Der Schalter daneben entscheidet, ob das beim Start geschieht. Hilfe → Changelog zeigt Fassung für Fassung, was behoben und hinzugekommen ist, in deiner Sprache - nach einem Update öffnet sie sich einmal von selbst."},{"p":"tasten.html","a":"","t":"Tastenkürzel","s":"Tastenkürzel","x":""},{"p":"tasten.html","a":"skript","t":"Tastenkürzel","s":"Skript","x":"Gewählten Befehl bearbeiten Enter Den in der Events-Liste gewählten Befehl einfügen Insert Löschen Delete Duplizieren Space Kopieren Ctrl+C Ausschneiden (auch Strg+T) Ctrl+X Einfügen Ctrl+V REM: auskommentieren / zurück (Strg+Rücktaste: Kommentar entfernen) Backspace Nach oben (Alt+Unten: nach unten), im selben Block Alt+Up Rückgängig (Strg+Y oder Strg+Umschalt+Z: wiederholen) Ctrl+Z Suchen; F3 / Umschalt+F3 nächster / voriger Ctrl+F Lesezeichen setzen; F2 / Umschalt+F2 nächstes / voriges Ctrl+F2 Eintrag und Kinder aufklappen (Strg+Num+: alles) Num+ Eintrag zuklappen (Strg+Num-: alles) Num-"},{"p":"tasten.html","a":"datei","t":"Tastenkürzel","s":"Dateien","x":"Dieses Handbuch öffnen F1 Öffnen Ctrl+O Speichern Ctrl+S Speichern unter (wie im Original-BehavEd) Ctrl+A Alle speichern Ctrl+Shift+S Sicherung; Alt+R wiederherstellen Alt+B Zuletzt geöffnete Dateien Alt+M Einstellungen; Alt+X beenden Alt+P"},{"p":"tasten.html","a":"karte","t":"Tastenkürzel","s":"Karte und Kamera","x":"Fliegen (Maus über der Ansicht); Q / E runter / hoch, Umschalt schneller; rechte Maus schaut umher W A S D Ansicht 1 merken (… 9); 1 … 9 springt zurück Ctrl+1 Beim Ziehen einer Entity: Ringe in 15-Grad-Schritten; mit eingestelltem Raster schaltet es das Raster aus, ohne rastet ein Pfeil auf 8 Einheiten Ctrl Alt+Ziehen einer Entity: erst kopieren Alt Beim Ziehen eines Flugziels oder einer Schlüsselraute: nur hoch und runter Shift Platzieren, Wegpunktwerkzeug oder Steuern abbrechen Esc Beim Steuern: Kameraschlüssel am Zeiger setzen Enter"},{"p":"tasten.html","a":"zeit","t":"Tastenkürzel","s":"Zeitleiste","x":"50 ms zurück / vor, Maus über der Zeitleiste (Umschalt: 1 s) Links / Rechts Zum Anfang / Ende (Maus über der Zeitleiste) Pos1 / Ende Beim Ziehen eines Blocks: nur diesen Block verschieben Alt"},{"p":"tasten.html","a":"fenster","t":"Tastenkürzel","s":"Fenster","x":"Oberflächengröße (über den Spuren der Zeitleiste: die Zeitleiste zoomen) Strg + Mausrad"},{"p":"begriffe.html","a":"","t":"Begriffe","s":"Begriffe","x":"ICARUS Das Skriptsystem des Spiels. Skripte sind Text (.txt) und laufen übersetzt (.ibi). .ibi Ein übersetztes Skript - das, was das Spiel wirklich ausführt. Übersetzen! erzeugt es. .bhc Die Befehlsbeschreibung: jeder Befehl, seine Felder und deren Auswahl. affect Ein Block, dessen Befehle an eine benannte Figur oder Entity gehen. task / do / dowait Eine benannte Gruppe von Befehlen; do startet sie nebenher, dowait wartet, bis sie fertig ist. wait Eine Pause in Millisekunden. Im Spiel endet sie ein Bild (50 ms) später als geschrieben. SET_NAVGOAL Schickt eine Figur zu einem waypoint_navgoal. NPC_spawner Die Entity, die eine Figur erscheinen lässt; NPC_type sagt welche, NPC_targetname benennt sie für Skripte. ref_tag Eine benannte Marke in der Karte - für Kamerapositionen und Blickziele. target_scriptrunner Startet ein Skript, wenn es benutzt wird (von einem Auslöser, einer anderen Entity oder einem Skript). func_static Ein Brush-Modell der Karte, das Skripte bewegen können - Schiffe, Türen, Plattformen. ROFF (.rof) Eine aufgezeichnete Bewegung: je Spielbild ein kleiner Schritt in Ort und Winkel. Siehe . .pk3 Ein Zip-Archiv, aus dem das Spiel seine Dateien liest. Eine Mission wird in eines gepackt. .ent Die Entities einer Karte in einer eigenen Datei; Movie Duels lässt die Karte und legt eigene Entities daneben. Movie Duels Ein großer Jedi-Academy-Mod mit Zwischensequenz-Missionen - der Hauptzweck dieses Programms."},{"p":"knoepfe.html","a":"","t":"Every button","s":"Every button","x":"Hover over any button in the program to see the same explanation as a tooltip. Buttons with a coloured frame are switches: on or off."},{"p":"knoepfe.html","a":"modus","t":"Every button","s":"The mode bar","x":"The strip at the far left switches what the window shows. The script stays the same in every mode. Ereignisse The Ereignisse list of every command and macro, the script tree, the action column - for writing scripts.  Mission The mission: the entity list and inspector, the map in 3D with the timeline below - for cameras, figures, entities and saving the mission.  Modell A character model with its animations - to find an animation and put it into the script. "},{"p":"knoepfe.html","a":"aktionen","t":"Every button","s":"The action column (Events mode)","x":"The action column, as in the original BehavEd. Löschen Removes the selected lines (Delete). Klonen Inserts a copy right below (Space). Kopieren / Ausschneiden / Einfügen Clipboard (Ctrl+C / X / V). Paste goes below the selection; text from other programs is accepted after a question. Auskommentieren Turns lines into comments and back (Backspace). Suchen The Find window (Ctrl+F): search by command or value, replace in one or all scripts.  Nach oben / Nach unten Moves the selection one line, inside its block (Alt+Up/Down). Rückgängig / Wiederherstellen Undo and redo. Right-click either one for the full history.  Neu / Öffnen An empty script / open a .txt or a compiled .ibi. Zuletzt Recently opened files (Alt+M). Anhängen Adds another script to the end of this one. Speichern / Alle sichern / Speichern unter Save this script, every changed tab, or under a new name. Exportieren Writes the script as plain text and opens it. Sicherung / Wiederherstellen Keeps a copy next to the script (.bak) / goes back to it (Alt+B / Alt+R). Typen zeigen Shows the value types in the tree. %g Kommazahlen Shows numbers short: 1000 instead of 1000.000. Makros falten Shows a macro as one line. + / - Expands or collapses every block. Übersetzen! Saves the script and writes the .ibi the game runs; green when it worked, red with the messages when not. "},{"p":"knoepfe.html","a":"kartenleiste","t":"Every button","s":"The map toolbar (Mission mode)","x":"The toolbar above the map.  Neue Mission Starts a mission on any map: player start, script runner, intro script and mission folder are created.   Mission laden Opens a mission from a .pk3: map, entities, every script in tabs, the figures.   Mission speichern Saves every script, writes the .ent, compiles and packs the .pk3 - after checking the mission.   Keine Mission The name of the open mission; a dot means unsaved changes. Hover for its folder.  Karten  Dateien Opens a map from disk or from a .pk3, a mission folder, or a separate .ent file. Skripte The scripts the map's entities point to - pick one to open it.  Entities Shows the entity markers: walk targets, marks, runners, spawners.  Namen Writes the names of entities and figures into the view.  Figuren Shows the script's figures, moved by the timeline.  Effekte Shows the effects of the map (fx_runner).  Glühen The glow of shaders marked glow, as r_DynamicGlow.  Dynamisches Licht Lightsabers and effect lights light up walls and figures.  Nebel The fog of the map, as the game draws it.  Himmel The sky; switched off you can look into the map from outside.  Durch die Kamera Shows what the camera sees - the selected camera command, or the camera at the playhead.   Draufsicht Looks straight down; a cut height hides ceilings.   NPC-Wegpunkte The NPC waypoint window: show, create and check the network.   Raster Snaps entities to 8 to 64 units while dragging and placing.  Ansicht einstellen Brightness, ambient light, detail, shadows, highlighting the active script's entities.   Statistik Frame rate, textures, triangles and graphics card values."},{"p":"knoepfe.html","a":"kacheln","t":"Every button","s":"The placement tiles","x":"The strip on the left edge of the map. Click a tile, then click on the floor - or drag the tile into the view. Shift places several, Esc stops.   Figur (NPC_spawner) A character that spawns: set NPC_type and a name.  Laufziel (waypoint_navgoal) A place a figure walks to (SET_NAVGOAL).  Kamera-/Blickmarke (ref_tag) A mark with a direction - for cameras (tag) and look targets.  Blickziel (target_position) A point to look at or to aim at.  Skriptstarter (target_scriptrunner) Runs a script when it is used - by a trigger, the player start or another script.  Effekt (fx_runner) Plays an effect file (.efx).  Klang (target_speaker) Plays a sound, once or in a loop.  NPC-Wegpunkt (waypoint) A point of the NPC navigation network.  Spielerstart (info_player_start) Where the player spawns."},{"p":"knoepfe.html","a":"inspektor","t":"Every button","s":"The entity inspector","x":"The inspector under the entity list.  Hinfliegen Flies the view to the entity.  Auf den Boden Puts it on the floor below, like DROPTOFLOOR in the game.  Duplizieren A copy - of every selected entity. Alt+drag in the view does the same.  Löschen Removes it.  Animieren Opens the Animation window for doors, platforms, ships and effects.   Rückgängig Undoes the last entity change (entities have their own history).  Wiederholen Redoes it.  Alle Schlüssel (roh) Shows every key as plain text. + Schlüssel Adds a key. Öffnen Next to a script key: opens the script - and creates it in the mission folder if it does not exist yet."},{"p":"knoepfe.html","a":"kamera","t":"Every button","s":"The camera bar","x":"Appears in the view when the camera is selected.  The camera bar above the selected shot.  Verschieben Arrows: move the shot along one axis, the box in the middle in the view plane.  Drehen Rings: turn the shot. Welt World or Local: the arrows follow the map axes or the camera.  Vorige Einstellung The previous shot.  Nächste Einstellung The next shot.  Auf Ansicht setzen Puts the shot where you are looking.  Steuern Sit in the shot and fly it; Enter sets a key.   Durch die Kamera Look through the camera.  Kameravorschau A small picture of the camera's view in the corner.  Neue Kameraeinstellung hier A new shot at your view, after the selected one.  Einstellung löschen Removes the shot."},{"p":"knoepfe.html","a":"zeitleiste","t":"Every button","s":"The timeline","x":"The transport bar of the timeline.  An den Anfang Back to the start of the script.  Abspielen Plays the scene - camera, figures, sound - in game time.  Schleife Starts again at the end.  Klang Plays the sounds while the timeline runs.  Mitfahren Moves the view along with the camera.  Herauszoomen Shows more time.  Hineinzoomen Shows less time, in more detail.  Figurenzeilen One row per figure: when each one walks, speaks and acts.  Ruhige Spuren Also shows rows where nothing happens.  waits Shows the waits as their own blocks.  Kamera hier einfügen Inserts a camera shot at the playhead. The time display switches between seconds and frames when you click it; the list next to the play button sets the speed. Drag blocks to move them in time - ."},{"p":"knoepfe.html","a":"modell","t":"Every button","s":"The model toolbar (Model mode)","x":"The toolbar above the model.  .glm öffnen Opens a .glm model from disk.  Aus .pk3 Opens a model from the game's archives.  NPCs Every character of the game - click one to load it as the game shows it.  .skin öffnen Loads a .skin for the model.  .gla laden Loads another skeleton / animation file (.gla).  Drehteller Turns the model slowly around itself.  Knochen Shows the skeleton.  Kappen zeigen Shows the caps of the surfaces where limbs attach.  Texturen Textures on or off.  Ansicht einpassen The whole model in view, from the front.  Kopieren In the animation list: copies the animation name.  Ins Skript Puts set ( SET_ANIM_BOTH, ... ) for the animation into the script. "},{"p":"befehle.html","a":"","t":"Every command","s":"Every command","x":"Commands are inserted from the Ereignisse list (double-click, drag or Insert) and changed in the Ereignis-Editor (double-click the line). Hover over a command in the list to read the help text the game's designers wrote for it. How to put them together: ."},{"p":"befehle.html","a":"liste","t":"Every command","s":"The commands of the Events list","x":"flush Clears every command still waiting for this entity - what an affect block with FLUSH does at its start. flush ( ) if / else Runs the block only if the comparison holds (=, , ! for *not equal*). else must follow right after an if. if ( $get( FLOAT, \"count\")$, $>$, $2$ ) loop Repeats its block; the number says how often, -1 means forever. loop ( 3 ) affect Sends the commands of its block to one entity - a figure, a ship, a door - by its name. FLUSH replaces what the entity was doing, INSERT adds to it. The script itself does not wait for the block. affect ( \"kyle\", FLUSH ) run Starts another script on the entity that runs this one. run ( \"taspir_tut/kyle_spawn\" ) wait Pauses for so many milliseconds - or, with a name, until that task is finished. wait ( 2000 ) waitsignal Pauses until some other script calls signal with the same name. Only one script can wait for a given signal. waitsignal ( \"door_open\" ) signal Wakes the script that waits for this name. signal ( \"door_open\" ) sound Plays a sound on a channel of the entity - CHAN_VOICE for dialogue, so the mouth moves. sound ( CHAN_VOICE, \"sound/chars/kyle/...\" ) move Moves an entity (a door, a platform, a ship) to a position - and, if given, to new angles - in so many milliseconds. The Animate window writes these for you (). move ( , , 2000 ) rotate Turns an entity to angles (pitch, yaw, roll) in so many milliseconds. rotate ( , 1000 ) use Uses an entity by name, as if the player pressed it - opens a door, fires a trigger. use ( \"door1\" ) kill Kills the entity with this name. kill ( \"stormie1\" ) remove Removes the entity with this name from the game. remove ( \"stormie1\" ) print Shows a text in the middle of the screen. print ( \"Hello\" ) rem A comment - does nothing in the game. Auskommentieren turns any line into one. rem ( \"camera starts here\" ) declare / free Declares a variable (FLOAT, STRING, VECTOR; at most 16 per map) - free gives the name back. declare ( FLOAT, \"count\" ) set Changes a value: an entity field (SET_NAVGOAL, SET_ANIM_BOTH, ... - see the full list below) or a declared variable. set ( SET_WALKING, \"true\" ) camera Controls the cutscene camera; the first value chooses what it does - see the next section. camera ( ENABLE ) task Declares a named group of commands - it does not run yet. task ( \"walk\" ) do Starts a task and goes on at once. do ( \"walk\" ) dowait Starts a task and waits until it is done - for a walk: until the figure has arrived. dowait ( \"walk\" ) play Plays a ROFF file on the entity of the current affect block - a recorded movement. play ( PLAY_ROFF, \"taspir_tut/roffs/ravensClaw\" ) A command marked with * in its help text (for example SET_NAVGOAL) finishes its task only when the action is done - that is what lets dowait wait for it."},{"p":"befehle.html","a":"kamera","t":"Every command","s":"camera ( ... ) - the camera commands","x":"The first value of camera chooses the command. behaved shows every one of them in the timeline under Kamera and plays it in the view. Times are in milliseconds. ENABLE - Puts game in camera mode DISABLE - Takes game out of camera mode ZOOM number, whole number Normal is 80, 10 is zoomed in, max is 120.  Second value is time in ms to take to zoom to the new FOV MOVE vector, whole number Move to a absolute vector origin or TAG(\"targetname\", ORIGIN) over time over number of milliseconds PAN vector, vector, whole number Pan to absolute angle from current angle in dir (no dir will use shortest) over number of milliseconds ROLL number, whole number Roll to relative angle offsets of current angle over number of milliseconds TRACK text, number, whole number Get on track and move at speed, last number is whether or not to lerp to the start pos FOLLOW text, number, whole number Follow ents with matching cameraGroup at angleSpeed, last number is whether or not to lerp to the start angle DISTANCE number, whole number Keep this distance from cameraGroup (if any), last number is whether or not to lerp to the start angle FADE vector, number, vector, number, whole number Fade from [start Red Green Blue], [Opacity] to [end Red Green Blue], [Opacity] (all fields valid ranges are 0 to 1) over [number of milliseconds] SHAKE number, whole number Intensity (0-16) and duration, in milliseconds PATH text Path to ROF file"},{"p":"befehle.html","a":"makros","t":"Every command","s":"Macros","x":"At the end of the Ereignisse list. A macro inserts several set commands at once; Makros falten shows it as one line. standOnly simply stands, ignores enemies & alerts 3 walkOnly simply walks, ignores enemies & alerts 5 runOnly simply runs, ignores enemies & alerts 5 standNoAlerts simply stands, ignores alerts 2 walkNoAlerts simply walks, ignores alerts 4 runNoAlerts simply runs, ignores alerts 4 standNoEnemies simply stands, ignores enemies 2 walkNoEnemies simply walks, ignores enemies 4 runNoEnemies simply runs, ignores enemies 4 standGuardNoChase looks for enemies, shoots at but doesn't chase them 3 patrolRun patrols in a run, chases enemies 5 patrolNoChase patrols, sticks to patrol route even when shooting enemy 3 patrolWalkNoChase patrols in a walk, sticks to walking patrol route even when shooting enemy 5 patrolRunNoChase patrols in a run, sticks to running patrol route even when shooting enemy 5 default resets to default behavior 6"},{"p":"befehle.html","a":"set","t":"Every command","s":"set ( SET_... ) - every field","x":"All fields set can change, grouped as in the game's own list (Q3_Interface.h). The description is the one the editor shows - Raven's own words. Type part of a name into the search box of this guide to find a field. Parm strings SET_PARM1 text Set entity parm1 Parm strings SET_PARM2 text Set entity parm2 Parm strings SET_PARM3 text Set entity parm3 Parm strings SET_PARM4 text Set entity parm4 Parm strings SET_PARM5 text Set entity parm5 Parm strings SET_PARM6 text Set entity parm6 Parm strings SET_PARM7 text Set entity parm7 Parm strings SET_PARM8 text Set entity parm8 Parm strings SET_PARM9 text Set entity parm9 Parm strings SET_PARM10 text Set entity parm10 Parm strings SET_PARM11 text Set entity parm11 Parm strings SET_PARM12 text Set entity parm12 Parm strings SET_PARM13 text Set entity parm13 Parm strings SET_PARM14 text Set entity parm14 Parm strings SET_PARM15 text Set entity parm15 Parm strings SET_PARM16 text Set entity parm16 Scripts and other file paths SET_SPAWNSCRIPT text *.txt\" # Script to run when spawned //0 - do not change these, these are equal to BSET_SPAWN, etc Scripts and other file paths SET_USESCRIPT text *.txt\" # Script to run when used Scripts and other file paths SET_AWAKESCRIPT text *.txt\" # Script to run when startled Scripts and other file paths SET_ANGERSCRIPT text *.txt\" # Script run when find an enemy for the first time Scripts and other file paths SET_ATTACKSCRIPT text *.txt\" # Script to run when you shoot Scripts and other file paths SET_VICTORYSCRIPT text *.txt\" # Script to run when killed someone Scripts and other file paths SET_LOSTENEMYSCRIPT text *.txt\" # Script to run when you can't find your enemy Scripts and other file paths SET_PAINSCRIPT text *.txt\" # Script to run when hit Scripts and other file paths SET_FLEESCRIPT text *.txt\" # Script to run when hit and low health Scripts and other file paths SET_DEATHSCRIPT text *.txt\" # Script to run when killed Scripts and other file paths SET_DELAYEDSCRIPT text *.txt\" # Script to run after a delay Scripts and other file paths SET_BLOCKEDSCRIPT text *.txt\" # Script to run when blocked by teammate Scripts and other file paths SET_FFIRESCRIPT text *.txt\" # Script to run when player has shot own team repeatedly Scripts and other file paths SET_FFDEATHSCRIPT text *.txt\" # Script to run when player kills a teammate Scripts and other file paths SET_MINDTRICKSCRIPT text *.txt\" # Script to run when player kills a teammate Scripts and other file paths SET_VIDEO_PLAY text *.roq\" # Play a video (inGame) Scripts and other file paths SET_CINEMATIC_SKIPSCRIPT text *.txt\" # Script to run when skipping the running cinematic Scripts and other file paths SET_RAILCENTERTRACKLOCKED text Turn off the centered movers on the given track Scripts and other file paths SET_RAILCENTERTRACKUNLOCKED text Turn on the centered movers on the given track Scripts and other file paths SET_SKIN text just blindly sets whatever skin you set!  include full path after \"base/\"... eg: \"models/players/tavion_new/model_possessed.skin\" Standard strings SET_ENEMY text Set enemy by targetname Standard strings SET_LEADER text Set for BS_FOLLOW_LEADER Standard strings SET_NAVGOAL text *Move to this navgoal then continue script Standard strings SET_CAPTURE text Set captureGoal by targetname Standard strings SET_VIEWTARGET text Set angles toward ent by targetname Standard strings SET_WATCHTARGET text Set angles toward ent by targetname, will *continue* to face them... only in BS_CINEMATIC Standard strings SET_TARGETNAME text Set/change your targetname Standard strings SET_PAINTARGET text Set/change what to use when hit Standard strings SET_CAMERA_GROUP text all ents with this cameraGroup will be focused on Standard strings SET_CAMERA_GROUP_TAG text What tag on all clients to try to track Standard strings SET_LOOK_TARGET text object for NPC to look at Standard strings SET_ADDRHANDBOLT_MODEL text object to place on NPC right hand bolt Standard strings SET_REMOVERHANDBOLT_MODEL text object to remove from NPC right hand bolt Standard strings SET_ADDLHANDBOLT_MODEL text object to place on NPC left hand bolt Standard strings SET_REMOVELHANDBOLT_MODEL text object to remove from NPC left hand bolt Standard strings SET_CAPTIONTEXTCOLOR text Color of text RED,WHITE,BLUE, YELLOW Standard strings SET_CENTERTEXTCOLOR text Color of text RED,WHITE,BLUE, YELLOW Standard strings SET_SCROLLTEXTCOLOR text Color of text RED,WHITE,BLUE, YELLOW Standard strings SET_COPY_ORIGIN text Copy the origin of the ent with targetname to your origin Standard strings SET_DEFEND_TARGET text This NPC will attack the target NPC's enemies Standard strings SET_TARGET text Set/change your target Standard strings SET_TARGET2 text Set/change your target2, on NPC's, this fires when they're knocked out by the red hypo Standard strings SET_LOCATION text What trigger_location you're in - Can only be gotten, not set! Standard strings SET_REMOVE_TARGET text Target that is fired when someone completes the BS_REMOVE behaviorState Standard strings SET_LOADGAME text Load the savegame that was auto-saved when you started the holodeck Standard strings SET_LOCKYAW text Lock legs to a certain yaw angle (or \"off\" or \"auto\" uses current) Standard strings SET_VIEWENTITY text Make the player look through this ent's eyes - also shunts player movement control to this ent Standard strings SET_LOOPSOUND text sound\\*.*\" # Looping sound to play on entity Standard strings SET_ICARUS_FREEZE text Specify name of entity to freeze - !!!NOTE!!! since the ent is frozen, you must have some other entity unfreeze it!!! Standard strings SET_ICARUS_UNFREEZE text Specify name of entity to unfreeze Standard strings SET_SABER1 text Name of a saber in sabers.cfg to use in first hand.  \"none\" removes current saber Standard strings SET_SABER2 text Name of a saber in sabers.cfg to use in second hand.  \"none\" removes current saber Standard strings SET_PLAYERMODEL text Name of an NPC config in NPC2.cfg to use for this ent Standard strings SET_VEHICLE text Name of an vehicle config in vehicles.cfg to make this ent drive Standard strings SET_SCROLLTEXT text key of text string to print Standard strings SET_LCARSTEXT text key of text string to print in LCARS frame Standard strings SET_CENTERTEXT text key of text string to print in center of screen. vectors SET_ORIGIN vector Set origin explicitly or with TAG vectors SET_ANGLES vector Set angles explicitly or with TAG vectors SET_TELEPORT_DEST vector Set origin here as soon as the area is clear vectors SET_SABER_ORIGIN vector Removes this ent's saber from their hand, turns it off, and places it at the specified location floats SET_XVELOCITY number Velocity along X axis floats SET_YVELOCITY number Velocity along Y axis floats SET_ZVELOCITY number Velocity along Z axis floats SET_Z_OFFSET number Vertical offset from original origin... offset/ent's speed * 1000ms is duration floats SET_DPITCH number Pitch for NPC to turn to floats SET_DYAW number Yaw for NPC to turn to floats SET_TIMESCALE number Speed-up slow down game (0 - 1.0) floats SET_CAMERA_GROUP_Z_OFS text when following an ent with the camera, apply this z ofs floats SET_VISRANGE number How far away NPC can see floats SET_EARSHOT number How far an NPC can hear floats SET_VIGILANCE number How often to look for enemies (0 - 1.0) floats SET_GRAVITY number Change this ent's gravity - 800 default floats SET_FACEAUX number Set face to Aux expression for number of seconds floats SET_FACEBLINK number Set face to Blink expression for number of seconds floats SET_FACEBLINKFROWN number Set face to Blinkfrown expression for number of seconds floats SET_FACEFROWN number Set face to Frown expression for number of seconds floats SET_FACENORMAL number Set face to Normal expression for number of seconds floats SET_FACEEYESCLOSED number Set face to Eyes closed floats SET_FACEEYESOPENED number Set face to Eyes open floats SET_WAIT number Change an entity's wait field floats SET_FOLLOWDIST number How far away to stay from leader in BS_FOLLOW_LEADER floats SET_SCALE number Scale the entity model floats SET_RENDER_CULL_RADIUS number Used to ensure rendering for entities with geographically sprawling animations (world units) floats SET_DISTSQRD_TO_PLAYER number Only to be used in a 'get'. (Distance to player)*(Distance to player) ints SET_ANIM_HOLDTIME_LOWER whole number Hold lower anim for number of milliseconds ints SET_ANIM_HOLDTIME_UPPER whole number Hold upper anim for number of milliseconds ints SET_ANIM_HOLDTIME_BOTH whole number Hold lower and upper anims for number of milliseconds ints SET_HEALTH whole number Change health ints SET_ARMOR whole number Change armor ints SET_WALKSPEED whole number Change walkSpeed ints SET_RUNSPEED whole number Change runSpeed ints SET_YAWSPEED whole number Change yawSpeed ints SET_AGGRESSION whole number Change aggression 1-5 ints SET_AIM whole number Change aim 1-5 ints SET_FRICTION whole number Change ent's friction - 6 default ints SET_SHOOTDIST whole number How far the ent can shoot - 0 uses weapon ints SET_HFOV whole number Horizontal field of view ints SET_VFOV whole number Vertical field of view ints SET_DELAYSCRIPTTIME whole number How many milliseconds to wait before running delayscript ints SET_FORWARDMOVE whole number NPC move forward -127(back) to 127 ints SET_RIGHTMOVE whole number NPC move right -127(left) to 127 ints SET_STARTFRAME whole number frame to start animation sequence on ints SET_ENDFRAME whole number frame to end animation sequence on ints SET_ANIMFRAME whole number frame to set animation sequence to ints SET_COUNT whole number Change an entity's count field ints SET_SHOT_SPACING whole number Time between shots for an NPC - reset to defaults when changes weapon ints SET_MISSIONSTATUSTIME whole number Amount of time until Mission Status should be shown after death ints SET_WIDTH whole number Width of NPC bounding box. ints SET_SABER1BLADEON whole number Activate a specific blade of Saber 1 (0 - (MAX_BLADES - 1)). ints SET_SABER1BLADEOFF whole number Deactivate a specific blade of Saber 1 (0 - (MAX_BLADES - 1)). ints SET_SABER2BLADEON whole number Activate a specific blade of Saber 2 (0 - (MAX_BLADES - 1)). ints SET_SABER2BLADEOFF whole number Deactivate a specific blade of Saber 2 (0 - (MAX_BLADES - 1)). ints SET_DAMAGEENTITY whole number Damage this entity with set amount. booleans SET_IGNOREPAIN BOOL_TYPES Do not react to pain booleans SET_IGNOREENEMIES BOOL_TYPES Do not acquire enemies booleans SET_IGNOREALERTS BOOL_TYPES Do not get enemy set by allies in area(ambush) booleans SET_DONTSHOOT BOOL_TYPES Others won't shoot you booleans SET_NOTARGET BOOL_TYPES Others won't pick you as enemy booleans SET_DONTFIRE BOOL_TYPES Don't fire your weapon booleans SET_LOCKED_ENEMY BOOL_TYPES Keep current enemy until dead booleans SET_CROUCHED BOOL_TYPES Force NPC to crouch booleans SET_WALKING BOOL_TYPES Force NPC to move at walkSpeed booleans SET_RUNNING BOOL_TYPES Force NPC to move at runSpeed booleans SET_CHASE_ENEMIES BOOL_TYPES NPC will chase after enemies booleans SET_LOOK_FOR_ENEMIES BOOL_TYPES NPC will be on the lookout for enemies booleans SET_FACE_MOVE_DIR BOOL_TYPES NPC will face in the direction it's moving booleans SET_DONT_FLEE BOOL_TYPES NPC will not run from danger booleans SET_FORCED_MARCH BOOL_TYPES NPC will not move unless you aim at him booleans SET_UNDYING BOOL_TYPES Can take damage down to 1 but not die booleans SET_NOAVOID BOOL_TYPES Will not avoid other NPCs or architecture booleans SET_SOLID BOOL_TYPES Make yourself notsolid or solid booleans SET_PLAYER_USABLE BOOL_TYPES Can be activateby the player's \"use\" button booleans SET_LOOP_ANIM BOOL_TYPES For non-NPCs, loop your animation sequence booleans SET_INTERFACE BOOL_TYPES Player interface on/off booleans SET_SHIELDS BOOL_TYPES NPC has no shields (Borg do not adapt) booleans SET_INVISIBLE BOOL_TYPES Makes an NPC not solid and not visible booleans SET_VAMPIRE BOOL_TYPES Draws only in mirrors/portals booleans SET_FORCE_INVINCIBLE BOOL_TYPES Force Invincibility effect, also godmode booleans SET_GREET_ALLIES BOOL_TYPES Makes an NPC greet teammates booleans SET_VIDEO_FADE_IN BOOL_TYPES Makes video playback fade in booleans SET_VIDEO_FADE_OUT BOOL_TYPES Makes video playback fade out booleans SET_PLAYER_LOCKED BOOL_TYPES Makes it so player cannot move booleans SET_LOCK_PLAYER_WEAPONS BOOL_TYPES Makes it so player cannot switch weapons booleans SET_NO_IMPACT_DAMAGE BOOL_TYPES Stops this ent from taking impact damage booleans SET_NO_KNOCKBACK BOOL_TYPES Stops this ent from taking knockback from weapons booleans SET_ALT_FIRE BOOL_TYPES Force NPC to use altfire when shooting booleans SET_NO_RESPONSE BOOL_TYPES NPCs will do generic responses when this is on (usescripts override generic responses as well) booleans SET_INVINCIBLE BOOL_TYPES Completely unkillable booleans SET_NO_COMBAT_TALK BOOL_TYPES NPCs will not do their combat talking noises when this is on booleans SET_NO_ALERT_TALK BOOL_TYPES NPCs will not do their combat talking noises when this is on booleans SET_TREASONED BOOL_TYPES Player has turned on his own- scripts will stop, NPCs will turn on him and level changes load the brig booleans SET_DISABLE_SHADER_ANIM BOOL_TYPES Allows turning off an animating shader in a script booleans SET_SHADER_ANIM BOOL_TYPES Sets a shader with an image map to be under frame control booleans SET_SABERACTIVE BOOL_TYPES Turns saber on/off booleans SET_ADJUST_AREA_PORTALS BOOL_TYPES Only set this on things you move with script commands that you *want* to open/close area portals.  Default is off. booleans SET_DMG_BY_HEAVY_WEAP_ONLY BOOL_TYPES When true, only a heavy weapon class missile/laser can damage this ent. booleans SET_SHIELDED BOOL_TYPES When true, ion_cannon is shielded from any kind of damage. booleans SET_NO_GROUPS BOOL_TYPES This NPC cannot alert groups or be part of a group booleans SET_FIRE_WEAPON BOOL_TYPES Makes NPC will hold down the fire button, until this is set to false booleans SET_FIRE_WEAPON_NO_ANIM BOOL_TYPES NPC will hold down the fire button, but they won't play firing anim booleans SET_SAFE_REMOVE BOOL_TYPES NPC will remove only when it's safe (Player is not in PVS) booleans SET_BOBA_JET_PACK BOOL_TYPES Turn on/off Boba Fett's Jet Pack booleans SET_NO_MINDTRICK BOOL_TYPES Makes NPC immune to jedi mind-trick booleans SET_INACTIVE BOOL_TYPES in lieu of using a target_activate or target_deactivate booleans SET_FUNC_USABLE_VISIBLE BOOL_TYPES provides an alternate way of changing func_usable to be visible or not, DOES NOT AFFECT SOLID booleans SET_SECRET_AREA_FOUND BOOL_TYPES Increment secret areas found counter booleans SET_END_SCREENDISSOLVE BOOL_TYPES End of game dissolve into star background and credits booleans SET_USE_CP_NEAREST BOOL_TYPES NPCs will use their closest combat points, not try and find ones next to the player, or flank player booleans SET_MORELIGHT BOOL_TYPES NPC will have a minlight of 96 booleans SET_NO_FORCE BOOL_TYPES NPC will not be affected by force powers booleans SET_NO_FALLTODEATH BOOL_TYPES NPC will not scream and tumble and fall to hit death over large drops booleans SET_DISMEMBERABLE BOOL_TYPES NPC will not be dismemberable if you set this to false (default is true) booleans SET_NO_ACROBATICS BOOL_TYPES Jedi won't jump, roll or cartwheel booleans SET_USE_SUBTITLES BOOL_TYPES When true NPC will always display subtitle regardless of subtitle setting booleans SET_CLEAN_DAMAGING_ENTS BOOL_TYPES Removes entities that could muck up cinematics, explosives, turrets, seekers. booleans SET_HUD BOOL_TYPES Turns on/off HUD booleans SET_NO_PVS_CULL BOOL_TYPES This entity will *always* be drawn - use only for special case cinematic NPCs that have anims that cover multiple rooms!!! booleans SET_CLOAK BOOL_TYPES Set a Saboteur to cloak (true) or un-cloak (false). booleans SET_FORCE_HEAL BOOL_TYPES Causes this ent to start force healing at whatever level of force heal they have booleans SET_FORCE_SPEED BOOL_TYPES Causes this ent to start force speeding at whatever level of force speed they have (may not do anything for NPCs?) booleans SET_FORCE_PUSH BOOL_TYPES Causes this ent to do a force push at whatever level of force push they have - will not fail booleans SET_FORCE_PUSH_FAKE BOOL_TYPES Causes this ent to do a force push anim, sound and effect, will not push anything booleans SET_FORCE_PULL BOOL_TYPES Causes this ent to do a force push at whatever level of force push they have - will not fail booleans SET_FORCE_MIND_TRICK BOOL_TYPES Causes this ent to do a jedi mind trick at whatever level of mind trick they have (may not do anything for NPCs?) booleans SET_FORCE_GRIP BOOL_TYPES Causes this ent to grip their enemy at whatever level of grip they have (will grip until scripted to stop) booleans SET_FORCE_LIGHTNING BOOL_TYPES Causes this ent to lightning at whatever level of lightning they have (will lightning until scripted to stop) booleans SET_FORCE_SABERTHROW BOOL_TYPES Causes this ent to throw their saber at whatever level of saber throw they have (will throw saber until scripted to stop) booleans SET_FORCE_RAGE BOOL_TYPES Causes this ent to go into force rage at whatever level of force rage they have booleans SET_FORCE_PROTECT BOOL_TYPES Causes this ent to start a force protect at whatever level of force protect they have booleans SET_FORCE_ABSORB BOOL_TYPES Causes this ent to do start a force absorb at whatever level of force absorb they have booleans SET_FORCE_DRAIN BOOL_TYPES Causes this ent to start force draining their enemy at whatever level of force drain they have (will drain until scripted to stop) booleans SET_WINTER_GEAR BOOL_TYPES Set the player to wear his/her winter gear (skins torso_g1 and lower_e1), or restore the default skins. booleans SET_NO_ANGLES BOOL_TYPES This NPC/player will not have any bone angle overrides or pitch or roll (should only be used in cinematics) calls SET_SKILL - Cannot set this, only get it - valid values are 0 through 3 Special tables SET_ANIM_UPPER ANIM_NAMES Torso and head anim Special tables SET_ANIM_LOWER ANIM_NAMES Legs anim Special tables SET_ANIM_BOTH ANIM_NAMES Set same anim on torso and legs Special tables SET_PLAYER_TEAM TEAM_NAMES Your team Special tables SET_ENEMY_TEAM TEAM_NAMES Team in which to look for enemies Special tables SET_BEHAVIOR_STATE BSTATE_STRINGS Change current bState Special tables SET_DEFAULT_BSTATE BSTATE_STRINGS Change fallback bState Special tables SET_TEMP_BSTATE BSTATE_STRINGS Set/Chang a temp bState Special tables SET_EVENT EVENT_NAMES Events you can initiate Special tables SET_WEAPON WEAPON_NAMES Change/Stow/Drop weapon Special tables SET_ITEM ITEM_NAMES Give items Special tables SET_MUSIC_STATE MUSIC_STATES Set the state of the dynamic music Special tables SET_FORCE_HEAL_LEVEL FORCE_LEVELS Change force power level Special tables SET_FORCE_JUMP_LEVEL FORCE_LEVELS Change force power level Special tables SET_FORCE_SPEED_LEVEL FORCE_LEVELS Change force power level Special tables SET_FORCE_PUSH_LEVEL FORCE_LEVELS Change force power level Special tables SET_FORCE_PULL_LEVEL FORCE_LEVELS Change force power level Special tables SET_FORCE_MINDTRICK_LEVEL FORCE_LEVELS Change force power level Special tables SET_FORCE_GRIP_LEVEL FORCE_LEVELS Change force power level Special tables SET_FORCE_LIGHTNING_LEVEL FORCE_LEVELS Change force power level Special tables SET_SABER_THROW FORCE_LEVELS Change force power level Special tables SET_SABER_DEFENSE FORCE_LEVELS Change force power level Special tables SET_SABER_OFFENSE SABER_STYLES Change force power level Special tables SET_FORCE_RAGE_LEVEL FORCE_LEVELS Change force power level Special tables SET_FORCE_PROTECT_LEVEL FORCE_LEVELS Change force power level Special tables SET_FORCE_ABSORB_LEVEL FORCE_LEVELS Change force power level Special tables SET_FORCE_DRAIN_LEVEL FORCE_LEVELS Change force power level Special tables SET_FORCE_SIGHT_LEVEL FORCE_LEVELS Change force power level Special tables SET_SABER1_COLOR1 SABER_COLORS Set color of first blade of first saber Special tables SET_SABER1_COLOR2 SABER_COLORS Set color of second blade of first saber Special tables SET_SABER2_COLOR1 SABER_COLORS Set color of first blade of first saber Special tables SET_SABER2_COLOR2 SABER_COLORS Set color of second blade of first saber Special tables SET_DISMEMBER_LIMB HIT_LOCATIONS Cut off a part of a body and send the limb flying Special tables SET_OBJECTIVE_SHOW OBJECTIVES Show objective on mission screen Special tables SET_OBJECTIVE_HIDE OBJECTIVES Hide objective from mission screen Special tables SET_OBJECTIVE_SUCCEEDED OBJECTIVES Mark objective as completed Special tables SET_OBJECTIVE_SUCCEEDED_NO_UPDATE OBJECTIVES Mark objective as completed, no update sent to screen Special tables SET_OBJECTIVE_FAILED OBJECTIVES Mark objective as failed Special tables SET_MISSIONFAILED MISSIONFAILED Mission failed screen activates Special tables SET_TACTICAL_SHOW TACTICAL Show tactical info on mission objectives screen Special tables SET_TACTICAL_HIDE TACTICAL Hide tactical info on mission objectives screen Special tables SET_OBJECTIVE_CLEARALL - Force all objectives to be hidden Special tables SET_OBJECTIVE_LIGHTSIDE - Used to get whether the player has chosen the light (succeeded) or dark (failed) side. Special tables SET_MISSIONSTATUSTEXT STATUSTEXT Text to appear in mission status screen Special tables SET_MENU_SCREEN MENUSCREENS Brings up specified menu screen Special tables SET_CLOSINGCREDITS - Show closing credits Special tables SET_LEAN LEAN_TYPES Lean left, right or stop leaning"},{"p":"befehle.html","a":"ausdruecke","t":"Every command","s":"Expressions: get, tag, random","x":"Instead of a fixed value, a field can hold an expression. In the editor, Helfer builds them: Get - get ( FLOAT, \"name\" ) reads a variable declared with declare. Tag - tag ( \"cam_door\", ORIGIN ) takes the position (or ANGLES) of a ref_tag on the map. That is how cameras stand on marks. Rnd - random ( 1000, 3000 ) a random number between two values, for example a wait."}];
